  ('zcrm_1579374000113412013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109794002', 'Sharri Maynard', NULL, '2-9-2023:  Sharri called - she wanted to update her pymt info.  She had not realized she can save money by using ACH, so we went over that &amp; she is chg''ing to a direct draw.  Walked her thru how to find &amp; comp the form.  Also, let her know this is in time for this month''s draw.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-02-09 16:13:44', '2023-02-09 16:13:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113395062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108399107', 'James Leo Durocher', NULL, '2-9-23 Leo called to help son Paolo, 37 get ins since his job just ended Feb. 1st. I instructed him to create a C4 account and select me as agent. Once he does we can finalize the Friday Silver plan choice. I let him know he will need to show proof of SEP. He needs a medication and I told him to go in and ask for the best cash price or get coupon on GoodRX. They will do that and let me know when they are ready to proceed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-09 15:40:52', '2023-02-09 15:40:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113411024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093898002', 'Matthew Hoit', NULL, '02.09.2023 Selina called to confirm they have coverage for daughter Aria, when she travels to Israel. I shared with her that Zion covers their members when they travel, and maybe you just want to give them a heads up. Selina asked if it is part of the plan or do they have to pay extra.
I consulted with Cari and she reiterated that it''s called International Catastrophic coverage/Medical Tourism and that it is just part of the plan. She also recommended that, in case anything happens though, have to them make sure they have our concierge # (Zion is open similar hours, so they could take their # for emergencies only, but we can help guide them.)
I gave Selina Zion''s number as well. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-09 15:30:45', '2023-02-09 15:30:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113395057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028522022', 'Matthew DePofi', NULL, '2-9-23 I talked with Jennifer and let her know that part of the wellness visit might be covered as long as it''s coded properly with the wellness/screening Z code. She gave me the correct # for Apex which is 1-800-795-7772.  Matt can call to make sure his colonoscopy from this past summer is paid for and he''s active. Patti sees him active in their system. So, that''s all set on that front!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-09 14:39:29', '2023-02-09 14:39:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113415006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080094010', 'Amy Jacobs-Schroeder', NULL, '02.09.23:  Sean emailed.  Said Tuesday morning would be good for them for a call to discuss Dental &amp; Vision options.  I scheduled us for 9 a.m. PST.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-02-09 14:18:25', '2023-02-09 14:18:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113395052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028522022', 'Matthew DePofi', NULL, '2-9-23 Matt explained to me that he went into his dr. for his annual wellness visit. They carried that out. Then he asked for an EKG just to check on things since he hadn''t done one in a while. He wants to see a cardiologist just to be safe. He''s upset since he''s now told none of the annual wellness visit/screening will be paid for by Apex. He tried calling Apex via Thomas''s encouragement from Sedera. He called Apex at 866-826-5317 and was told it''s a company called HM that works with 7 different companies. They told him to call Apex directly and it was the same # he had called initially to reach the person he was already talking with. He also said HM couldn''t find him in the system which is what happened last summer when he got a colonoscopy done and had a $1000+ bill from BCH that was a fight to get paid. He wants to make sure he''s in the Apex system as a member still since it was such a nightmare and still is ongoing with challenges. 
I explained that part of his wellness visit might be covered by Apex as long as his doctor coded it as wellness and not diagnostic. That will be up to the dr. I will find out the best # to call Apex and let him know if it''s different. I will ask to make sure he''s showing up in Apex''s system. If not, it will be resolved since he''s an active paying member. He now understands why the MPB Concierge Team is recommending clients to open a Need immediately since there''s a 6 month time limit from the date of service. This will ensure that doesn''t lapse as he reaches his $1000 IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-09 14:03:48', '2023-02-09 14:03:48'),
