  ('zcrm_1579374000113380021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073887226', 'Dennis Barela', NULL, '02.08.2023 Cristi called requesting we help negotiate a bill from her mamm. preventative visit. She shared that her mamm is not being covered by Planstin, and they are saying it is because it is a different kind of mamm. AND they did ultrasounds too. They reduced her bill by 200, bill is $1899.90. Cristi also shares that she''s always had a mamm each vs every other year, and has been covered.
Total concerns Cristi shared are:
1-What is her accurate ID#? The one on the Planstin card and the one on the invoice are not the same.
2-Negotiate/Cover a mamm bill.
3-On her present bill and her past bill it says: 3D Type of Mamm. HOWEVER, the office from the LAST visit told her this 3D mamm is different.  AND they proceeded with ultrasounds at the same visit. 
I consulted with Jen and Cari via teams, and they were both helpful, as usual, recommending that Planstin will need to answer the "WHY?" the visit was not covered.
Per Cari''s guidance, I coached Cristi on what to say when she calls Planstin:
1-Ask Planstin: What is my accurate ID#, What does it show as my mbr ID#?
2-Don''t mention last years, say LAST TIME it was covered why not this TIME.
3-Were the mamm and ultrasound coded preventative?

Planstin shared with Cristi that her member/group ID# is not important, because she''s part of MPB. They also shared it was not covered, because they were coded as diagnostic.
I then coached Cristi to gather her invoices, receipts and any notes from that specific incident and scan them into PDF form. To then call us back and we will guide her with opening a medical need with Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-08 10:24:24', '2023-02-08 12:58:58'),
