  ('zcrm_1579374000112922057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537054', 'Michael Sharpe', NULL, '2-2-23 Micheal sent me some emails stating as follows:

Wendy,

Thanks for the well wishes. I have to say, however, that the news about the monthly pricing is surprising and unwelcome. I based my decision to continue with Sedera not entirely but partially upon the price I was given during enrolment and budgeted for this year accordingly. Additionally, I received no email on 11/29 stating a different monthly contribution. Finally, the $262.28 Monthly Contribution is still posted on my account page with the billing date of 3/1/23. Since this was the amount presented during enrollment and the amount still posted on my account home page, it is the amount I expect will be withdrawn, no more. Additionally, I expect that I will be refunded any monies taken from my account thus far in 2023 over and above this “Monthly Contribution.”

 

Please call with any questions or to discuss further (504) 319-9099.

Regards,

Michael Sharpe

My response after talking with Patti, "Hi Michael,

 

I just checked your account and verified with the Admin team that your account is one of the few that isn''t currently getting forced to upgrade. So, that is why you didn''t receive any of the emails I was referring to. Your monthly contribution is and has been $378 all along. That is remaining the same. The monthly contribution you see in your Sedera portal is super misleading and confusing. That is only the portion of your monthly membership fee that is going directly to member sharing. That fee does not include any of the other benefits that are part of your membership and it does not include the admin fees, etc. If you look at your bank account, you''ll see the $378 membership fee all along. I apologize for the false alarm!

Please let me know if you have any other questions.

 

Best wishes, 

 

Wendy Scipione"

Mike''s response - "Wendy,

I was forced, receiving numerous reminders to complete the process, even after I already had, to upgrade and spent a great deal of time and frustration going through the process.

 

As for the monthly contribution, I know what is being taken from my checking account. I also know the amount that your system told my I would be charged monthly. These numbers should match. Until they do, I expect to be charged what is shown on my account page as the amount due, no more, since that is the amount presented during enrollment and to this day.

 

Mike"

My final response - 

"Hi Michael,

I''ve tried calling you a few times and it doesn''t seem to work. I called this # 985-652-8228. I can''t seem to leave a vm. In reviewing your account, you have been charged $378 since inception with your start date of Aug. 1st of 2020. The amount you see in your Sedera account is never going to match your actual monthly membership fee because it is only the portion of the monthly fee that goes directly to the member-to-member sharing. Please call me if you have further questions.

Thanks,

Wendy Scipione"

MPB hasn''t changed his pricing on our end or cancelled his old plan to migrate to the new one. However Sedera seems to have forced the migration as stated for all memberships with MPB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-02 16:28:42', '2023-02-02 16:28:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112929028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111229010', 'Kelly Hughes', NULL, '02.02.2023 Kelly called to learn better how to proceed with POSSIBLY HAVE BROKEN her foot.
She can move it, but cannot put weight on it, it hurts.
She is interested in trying CirrusMD first to avoid Urgent Care, but wanted to know more about how to find someone in her area that would not reject her as a cash-patient, due to not having traditional insurance.
With Cari''s guidance via teams, I told her to present as ''cash-pay'', ask for a ''cash-pay'' discount, offer to pay her $1000 IUA and ask them to bill the balance.  
Kelly wanted to make sure she is set up in CirrusMD, and was ready to proceed with them first. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-02 16:11:14', '2023-02-02 16:11:14'),
