  ('zcrm_1579374000112645029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058401239', 'emmett murphy', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 2805 Question : I have had mbp health for several years but have never used it. wondering if there is a tutorial on how it works', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-01-31 07:18:06', '2023-01-31 07:18:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112663003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109742009', 'Bridgett Mansfield', NULL, '1-30-2023:  Did not talk w/Bridgett, so I sent an e-mail making her aware 1) how to request reimb &amp; 2) I plan to talk w/her after getting better direction so we can help her sub a ''med need''.      - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-31 01:04:20', '2023-02-06 10:53:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112639008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111955009', 'Abram Dunaway', NULL, '1-23-23 "I am received a call from my doctor and will need to schedule an appointment to review medical records. They won’t go through this over the phone. I am setting up an appointment soon.

In the meantime, I heard back from my current insurance company. Since my last day is Feb 3rd, I will be covered until the end of Feb. How can I make my effective date with MPB March 1st? This will give me a few more weeks to try and clear my records.

Thanks!

Abe"

We moved his start date back to March 1st bc he learned his coverage goes through the end of Feb. even with end date of work Feb. 5 (If I remember correctly).  We await his visit with his dr.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 21:42:05', '2023-01-30 21:43:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112639003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111955009', 'Abram Dunaway', NULL, '1-19-23 Good morning Wendy,

Following up on our conversation on pre-existing conditions. I should hear back from my doctor today on if he is willing to give me a clean bill of health for a prostate screening several months ago. 

If he is unwilling, I’d like to talk options with you. I saw in the literature that after the first year, there are some cost sharing opportunities. Can you tell me more about this?

My concern here is that I will not be fully covered in the future if something were to develop dealing with prostate issues. In that case, this plan would not be an option for me. I still have a couple weeks of original coverage and then can go on Cobra to keep my original plan. If I needed to cancel mpb due to this lack of coverage, what would that process look like?', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 21:41:25', '2023-01-30 21:41:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000167696', 'Rachel Weitz', NULL, '1-30-23 Hi Wendy,

I spoke to them again last week, there is a ticket that''s open and they say they''re still waiting to take care of it, but all previous tickets that were closed said we should have the 1/1 start date, and they tell me they''re still working on making that happen. So I''m still waiting to see what happens with these tickets.

And just to have it in one place, the most recent current and I believe only active ticket is 230120-000535.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 20:18:58', '2023-01-30 20:18:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112555086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089109010', 'Rick Sanders', NULL, '01.30.2023 Rick called to cancel. Was concerned about getting charged next month, and if any prorate is available. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-30 18:00:34', '2023-01-30 18:00:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043491580', 'Francis Lanzano', NULL, '1-30-23 I sent this to John to resolve. "Hi John,

It looks like you erroneously cancelled and reinstated Francis Lanzano on 12/23/22 per your notes. However, the billing on his account stopped at that same time. He was last billed on 11/20/22. The only reason I discovered this is because he''s one of my final clients who needs to complete the upgrade process with Sedera. How would you like to handle this client''s missing payments moving forward?  We are missing payments for 12/20 and 1/20. He might change his IUA now moving forward as well. I''ll have him complete the Change Form if he chooses to do so. I can let him know both payments were put on hold due to his need to upgrade to keep his account to remain active. 

Please let me know when you correct this."

Since John is away until Wed., I let Francis know that his payment/account was put on hold until his membership was upgraded with Sedera. He will do that after work hours tonight. He''s considering changing his IUA from $500 to $1000 or $1500. He knows to select Yes to the DPC/VPC question when upgrading.  He knows the price showing on Sedera is not his membership fee. He knows to let me know if he changes his IUA bc he''ll have to complete one more form so MPB will know his chosen IUA as well. Once this is all complete, he''ll be back in compliance and fully Active.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 17:00:18', '2023-01-30 17:00:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112609027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022809040', 'Pamela Finch', NULL, '1-30-2023:  Nahla brought me into the above conversation.  All treatment so far has been thru her chiropractor: ultrasound, accupuncture, decompression treatment, massage, etc. (approx $1600?).  When they started she couldn''t walk & at least she''s somewhat better, but they''ve gotten her as far as they can, so the next step is an MRI.  She''s a consultant & this is limiting her ability to earn, so very important issue.  She started w/chiropractic thinking if it took care of the issue, she''d be under her $2500 IUA.
     - Pamela is going to start a ''med need'' w/Zion.  She got a super bill with all the care she''s had to date to upload.  She knows chiropractic generally requires pre-approval & as part of a larger ''need'', so I''m not sure how they will handle it (towards her $2500 IUA?).  At least she''s prepared if they do not consider it towards her IUA.
     - She''s in that weird period, where memb do not have access to HCBB (8/1/2020).  I ran the fair price for the Spine MRI in 2 areas she''s looking at treatment and looked at the 2 facilities the doc has sugg.  She''d really like access to HCBB if at all poss because she''s going to be looking for diff doc/srvcs soon.  I sent a Teams chat to John Kach to see if we can get that for her.  Otherwise, she knows we can run the info for her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-30 16:42:15', '2023-01-30 17:29:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112609019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080945002', 'Macay Hunter', NULL, '1-30-2023:  Macay called, he''s wondering if their pediatrician suggested speach therapy, would that be covered?  They are thinking their son (19mos old) is delayed in his speach.  The guidelines are very clear on pg 19:  
     34. Speech Therapy
                   Speech therapy in relation to a shareable illness, injury, or accident is shareable for 35 outpatient visits per condition, up to $3,000. Speech therapy for conditions such as speech delays or learning impairments not caused by injury or accident is not shareable.

     He thought it was odd they would help w/an accident, but not learning.  I let him know my daughter was fluent at 12mos, then my son at 3 yrs refused to speak, but by 3yrs, 3mos, used a huge vocabulary.  So to ck w/the doc.  He/she will know better if they need to be concerned.
     He seemed frustrated enough, I said: you can try to submit the ''need'', but it''s pretty clear in the guidelines, so I would not expect a diff answer.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-30 16:30:09', '2023-01-30 16:30:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109372147', 'Aimee Day', NULL, '1-30-23 Aimee wants to change her IUA now depending on cost to lower it to $2500 IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 15:50:02', '2023-01-30 15:50:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112555060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098470009', 'Adam Ferro', NULL, '01.30.2023 Wants to cancel. I forwarded him to JC. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-30 15:41:33', '2023-01-30 15:41:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112555046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109568001', 'Donald Whitfield', NULL, '01.30.2023 Donald has problems with his knee, went to ER last Tuesday did x-rays, and orthopedic today did x-rays for more details, and want to schedule him an MRI.
Guided him to complete a medical need, needed to attain his Zion member number, so I transferred him over after our call.
He will get his number from them, ask them if he can submit his request without any receipts yet. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-30 15:11:10', '2023-01-30 15:32:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112555041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022809040', 'Pamela Finch', NULL, '01.30.2023 Pam has been seeing a chiro for the last 3 months for a disc problem, now it looks like she will need an MRI, and it might go over her IUA. Have not seen enough improvement. So now an MRI is in order.
11/7/2022 initial visit.
Are chiro visits count as part of the medical need now?
I consulted with Cari via teams. She asked: How much out of pocket is Pam so far? Pam said around $1600 between chiro and treatments. Cari did share alternative treatments are usually part of a larger need, but we can proceed to generating a medical need and upload all the receipts (superbill).
Pamela is not able to access - - - - - -. Cari is going to check with John Kach.
Cari proceeded to search fair pricing in HCBB. Rayus is where she would get her MRI at. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-30 15:00:53', '2023-01-30 17:08:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110457002', 'Christine Carlo', NULL, 'Welcome call completed! JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-01-30 14:55:42', '2023-01-30 14:55:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045739067', 'Rachel Namordi', NULL, '1-30-23 Sent to Patti just now, Rachel Namordi''s payment went through. She''s billed correctly at $462.24, but the fee above in Admin123 is showing $448.78. Those are usually matching.  This is the first time I haven''t seen it match.
Rachel is interested in using Cloud Medical but then she''d lose the chiro care, ACA compliant annual wellness visit (but have Sedera''s sharing for high cost item with caps and waiting periods) and she''ll lose unlimited PCP visits but instead have Dr. Tusek. He has a waiting list now as well. However, if she changes the IUA from $500 to $1000 it will bring her cost from $462.24 down to $374.78 at $1000. She''s considering that. But, she has a hypothyroid issue newly since enrolling and a current torn glute issue she''s managing for about 1 year with up to $3500 in PT with Sedera. So, she doesn''t want to move at this point. Makes most sense to just change the IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 14:46:04', '2023-01-30 14:46:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112609008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112123001', 'Joy Sundberg', NULL, '1-30-2023:  Joy called to conf her memb did get setup for a 2/1/2023 eff date.  I can see in Admin123 her eff is 2/1/23 (they had corrected on the backside).  I assured her she''s set, went over how to present in case she needs to for a catastrophic item because she was concerned she doesn''t have a card.  Went into education lightly since she has a ''Welcome Call'' on the 6th:  no ins, ''cash-pay'', ask for disc, offer to pay 1k IUA & can they bill for balance, call us & we''ll help her start a ''med need'' w/the healthsharing comp.
     - Also, went over how to cancel when she ages into Medicare on 9/1/2023.  She''s grateful to have this healthcare for the 7-mos prior to that for protection.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-30 14:43:17', '2023-01-30 15:29:51'),
