  ('zcrm_1579374000112555013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063775002', 'Daniel Gutierrez', NULL, '01.30.2023 Martha called to get a prescription quote for her husband, Daniel Gutierrez.
The PA who performed the annual exam, did not like the look on his right leg, a long time ago motorcycle accident, blood clotting, leg is purple, she urged him to go see an orthopedic. Martha suggested to see a vein specialist instead.
They went to the vein specialist and the dr there, was a very informative, and less expensive.
They started the blood clotting, one month supply of medicine (Eliquis), through the introductory plan of the vein specialty place, 
They need to get refills on Eliquis, 90 more days, to continue to monitor the blood clot. The second visit they observed a vein/artery is 20% blockage. But they did not measure the first time visit.
I guided her to the Member Portal and Updates to the RX Quote form. She will put the Brand name of the medicine but is ok with generic. Wants the option to buy 60 days if the 90 days is too expensive. 
Because the RX quote is very expensive, I called Martha for more options:
Contact our international shopper for 120
Find 60 from a local pharmacy (since Reid takes about 4 weeks) OR see if her doctor has an samples for those 30 days. 
I was able to get her a quote from Reid: Eliquis 5mg x 112 tabs $151.16 + $9.95 shipping. And she had found a coupon for 30 days at her local pharmacy. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-30 13:01:50', '2023-01-31 10:25:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112555008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610497', 'Adam Burstein', NULL, '01.30.2023 Adam called to get clarification on how to proceed towards a mammogram.
