  ('zcrm_1579374000112391150', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075689380', 'Julie Wilson', NULL, '1-27-2023:  Julie called.  She''s having a health issue & needed direction:
     - First, she saw in her memb port a cancellation & chg of plan.  She was worried. I assured her that was due to the age band rate change & her acct looks fine.
     - Health issues, trying to get help.  PCP has done some lab work, several Urg Care Visits, etc.  First went in on: 1/4/2023.  Knows 6-mo deadline.  PCP, Neurologist, Endocrinologist - went over HCBB together & walked her thru how  it works, the ratings, fair price, etc.  She knows for this type of issue, it''s healthsharing & she''s resp for 1k IUA.  Will call us in April (unless knows it is going over the 1k sooner) & we can share how to sub the ''med need''.  She wondered about referral system, so we disc "med nec" is at her & her doc''s discretion, so a letter showing medical neccesity could be nec.  Referrals may be req''d by the specialist, but not by the healthsharing (it''s diff than ''ins'' there).  
        Knows to present for this issue w/NO card, NO Ins = ''Cash-Pay'' pt, ask for disc. try to pay as close to the 1k as poss, save all receipts, inv, etc.  Knows alt care req pre-appr & we''ll walk thru that w/her if that''s where they go.
     - Spoke lightly about ''P''lanstin = ''Prev'' care.  PCP she saw (Amanda DuBois) is NOT in ntwk.  She did establish a relationship to get some care for the above issue.  Knows to keep receipts since had to establish the relationship for her ''med need'' issue, but I also warned, they may or may not allow a med coded ''prev care'' visit twds the IUA, Zion will be the ones who would determin that.  Did let her know she can appeal, letting them know the only reason she saw her was for the issue as well.
     - Disc RBP pricing coming & that could help down the road for ''prev care''.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-27 16:27:26', '2023-01-27 17:12:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112431046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112433041', 'Helen Gordon', NULL, '1-28-23 Helen is in the middle of cancer surgeries and such and her drs. have moved out of the network. She thought she could just upgrade her plan but it''s too late. She was locked out of her account and was able to get it working again today finally.   She sees Dr. Sara Robinson who is in network. But, Dr. Mark Lorne Rosenblatt and Dr. Kevin Robert Berg are both no longer in the network. Since she''s their patient already, I recommended she talks with the drs. to see if they''ll still accept her insurance since she has a surgery upcoming on Feb. 14th. That gave her a path to follow rather than just a No. She can''t exactly change doctors at this point. She was considering trying to qualify for Medicaid but also doesn''t know if they accept Medicaid either. 
