  ('zcrm_1579374000112296063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029364085', 'Kristy Tripp', NULL, '1-25-23 I talked with Kristy and explained everything from the notes above. She knows to create a new Need for her recent mammo and ultrasound bc she has another follow up soon for that. She will not bother submitting the thermogram. She was forced to do a mammo simply to get the ultrasound she wanted. She also needs a colonoscopy in the next few years on the 5 year plan which will be diagnostic as well. She will create a new Need for that when the time comes. ACA compliant wellness wouldn''t have helped for any of this. Finally she thought her husband who is 46 needed a colonoscopy soon assuming since they lowered the age to 45 that he needed one. But, that''s only for high risk patients which he is not. He will wait until he''s 50. So, the ACA compliant wellness wouldn''t have done them any good anyhow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-25 16:29:42', '2023-01-25 16:29:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112221020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111992001', 'Lars Ensign', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 2772 Question : If I have a dentist appointment for checkup/cleaning or an annual recheck eye exam do I send in the receipts for those kinds of visits?

Left Lars a detailed vm and sent him an email regarding this information. ~JTS', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-01-25 16:25:05', '2023-01-26 12:11:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112296058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108662001', 'Juan Soto', NULL, '1-25-23 Susie Soto emailed out of frustration in getting meds. I responded via email and it got bounced back. This was my written response which I ended up telling her on the phone.

Hi Susie,

You should not be using your Planstin card for drugs. Planstin is to be presented ONLY for your annual wellness visit. You need to contact the MPB Concierge Team for assistance in getting all medications at the best price possible. They price out all medications in 5 or 6 different partner companies.  Every medication is different as to the best way to access it.  You will pay for the medications if it''s a maintenance medication. If it''s for an open Need, the cost will count towards your IUA and it will be shared in full above your IUA for all eligible medical expenses. What often happens is that the cash price of a medication is less than a co-pay with many plans. 

Please contact the MPB Concierge Team at 1-800-519-2969 for assistance.
____

She gets is now. He was told his med was $50 and then when he went to Walgreens they said it''s $140. So, he left and usually gets it through Canadian Pharmacy online but it takes 3 weeks. So, they will call the MPB Concierge Team for help to get it quicker and at a good price.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-25 16:11:09', '2023-01-25 16:11:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112296047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112304001', 'Lynn Ware', NULL, '1-25-23 Lynn is enrolling now into SECURE ES $1000/$625. She has asthma per the above genetic issue.  However, she''s never had any symptoms or treatment.  She completed the enrollment. I''m requesting a Feb. 1st start date from Patti. Lynn will do the Welcome Call. She might have more questions and will call me. She rushed a little to get in for Feb. 1st. She needs a little time to absorb it all. Super nice! He kids went to St. Lawrence and Williams College. She''s doing more xc skiing now and coaching which feels like an easier way to get exercise than waiting on lifts and in lines to ski. She''s happy she''s not paying nearly double for reg ins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-25 15:45:48', '2023-01-25 15:58:49'),
