  ('zcrm_1579374000112289003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108662001', 'Juan Soto', NULL, '1-25-2023:  Kinesha from Walgreens called.  She wanted ''Pharmacy Benefits''.  Juan is there to pickup some eyedrops:  Simbrinza 8ml x 1 (he has refills). 
     I priced locally & the best is still super expensive ~ $188.80 at CVS in Target.  Walgreens is quoting him $190-something as their regular price & the best disc Walg coupon I can find is ~$211.  
     Ck''d w/Reid, he can source at: Simbrinza 1%/0.2% x (3) 5ml bottles $129.49 + $9.95 shipping
     According to Juan, he called Planstin & they told him this would be $54.50 (I''m assuming thru OptumRX).  He thought Kinesha called Planstin when she called us.  He''s going to go back over & have her call Planstin (the # is on his Planstin Card) for the quoted price.  In the meantime, I called Kinesha w/instructions
     - Juan also says he no longer has an MPB.Health card, so I sent a Teams chat to Kelly F to reorder new cards for him & his spouse.     - CA

Crystal from Planstin, she''s confiming NO RX benefits, even though she can see someone quoted him $54.50 earlier.  She''s going to call Juan & let him know they misquoted him?  I let her know our best pricing above.     - CA

I sent Juan Reid''s quote info & contact info, as well as the cheapest coupon I found (see above).  I did send a Teams chat to Jennifer to discuss in her next Planstin meeting (I think it''s after she takes the Lead position).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-25 12:07:11', '2023-01-25 23:56:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112287011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109742009', 'Bridgett Mansfield', NULL, '01.25.2023 Bridgett called from the urgent care she took her son to, due to 104 degree temperature, lethargy and not being able to walk.
Bridgett is very new, has not had her WC, does not know how to maneuver the OPD plan.
She called to get guidance on how to make sure she is covered by us. I consulted Cari on this via teams, and she coached me on the same steps as we would with anything with Zion medical cost sharing.
Bridgett also wanted to know about using a card in order to get covered, since she could not find a doctor in the DPC yet. I was confused, so I brought Cari in, where she explained the above process about Zion and billing. S', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-25 11:56:19', '2023-01-25 11:56:19'),
