  ('zcrm_1579374000111768043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059755162', 'Scott Yarbrough', NULL, '1-16-2023:  Scott called & asked for me (I wasn''t in yet), so I called him back.  His surg $3700, Hosp $38372.77 (w/discount upfront = -$4988.46 = $33384.34)  or pay 25% & they''ll do the surgery with you making payments.  He got his ''med need'' submitted just last Friday & surgery is basically less than 3-weeks out, so I do not believe there''s time to get the need approved & go thru CareConnect.  He knows:
     - IF they decide it''s being assumed this is pre-x, they will share up to 50k since he''s at that point in the phase-in process.  If they say that, he may send specifics back as an appeal for the future: Years ago had issues, it healed & has been fine since ________ (= > the 24 mos look back period of his memb eff date per Scott), then it recently (date: ________, he thinks about 3 mos ago) started bothering him again, but should not be pre-x.
     - Also knows that if the surgery, & all treatments incl those he''s already pd for, PT afterwards etc. go over the 50k + $2500 IUA, he would be resp past that if they assume the pre-x AND if he gets near the renewal for 12/1/2023, past that date he may have further sharing available.
     - He sees the surgeon next wk & will ask if PT afterwards will be req''d.  If so, he will try to get the Treatment Plan to submit right away to make that approval process faster too.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-16 14:04:00', '2023-01-16 17:59:08'),
