  ('zcrm_1579374000111701013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095912017', 'Alicia Hutchens', NULL, '1-13-22 Talked with Alicia about her NLG policy and the Supplemental Term Life Policy offered by her company. They give her guaranteed issue up to $150K at no cost to her. She can pay more to increase it. I suggested leaving her NLG policy intact so if/when she leaves her company she is still protected and at the best rate bc she locked it in at a lower age. She won''t have to pay for her additional $150K from work, so it''s a win-win for her while she''s employed by them. She''s happy to keep it simple and do that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-13 11:37:21', '2023-01-13 11:37:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111701008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779071', 'Ruth Glas', NULL, '1-13-23 Ruth had a few more final questions. She''s looking at SECURE or DIRECT at $1000 IUA level. She''s considering adding reg ins and also looking at some other healthshares. Those aren''t as promising. She also appreciates my willingness to answer ALL of her questions. She will let me know either way next week on Tues or Wed what her decision is. I let her know about the 6 month limit to submit a Need and she will never be that person to wait. I also let her know of the extra $500 fee if you go to ER more than once for the same medical issue. She understands. Also, let her know about pre-approval for alternative care which she appreciates since reg ins never covers that. She totally understands to start with MPB Concierge Team for all scenarios. She is not self-employed but husband is with ASHI and I will waive $100 of the $125. I just called back and reminded her of that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-13 11:22:07', '2023-01-20 09:58:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111720003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059755162', 'Scott Yarbrough', NULL, '1-13-2023:  Scott called.  He''s having rotater cuff surgery 2/2/2023.  He doesn''t know exactly when he injured it.  Hurt for a few days, then would heal, etc...  $2500 IUA - has pd > 1k, PT to see if it would fix the issue, an MRI, etc., all w/in the last 3 mos.  We went over options if it is a pre-x vs not, phase in, this is his 3rd yr of membership so worst case scenario, he''ll have 50k.  The doc''s off will call him w/estimated amount & he''ll call if all exp look > that amt.
     - He''s so far into the process, I don''t know that there is time or opportunity to get the Care Connect team involved.  If the full expenses will be > 50k, we may want to talk to him about adjusting things?
     - Sent him the temp for sub a ''med need'' & walked him how to get it started.  It''s extremely time sensitive, so he''s going to try to get it in today.
     - Encouraged him to use the concierge service first (as traffic directors)  He''s been using his advisor Misty Berryman for that & I pointed out that this ''med need'' should have been started already so we had the approval, so that''s something she might not realize.  He seemed to understand that.  Hopefully, he''ll start using the concierge team so we can guide him in a better manner.     - CA

Scott called back for further guidance.  He''s all set now I think.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-13 11:07:01', '2023-01-13 14:36:35'),
