  ('zcrm_1579374000111591168', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091076002', 'Ernest Curry', NULL, 'Chris'' new e-mail (he''s sub form):    eccurry@aol.com *

1-12-2023:  Chris sent an e-mail w/mult items:
     - First, he summarized that since Zion will not give him a determination on whether his issue will be pre-x, he may be left not knowing unless/until something happens.  I resp: yes, it seems that our team has differing opinions - we do not see the ''med needs''. do not make the final determination, so it will be up to them if/when he submits a ''med need'' they feel is linked to his issue(s).
     - His asst Jason e-mailed me his colonoscopy records after I specified in our 12/28/2022 conv that he must call us & we will show him how to sub a ''med need''.  I resp on 1/10/2023 that it cannot be handled by us, he must call us for instructions (last week was a short holiday week & Jennifer was sick, so my reply was slower than I''d have liked = 6 bus days), but have not heard back from Jason to go over how to start a ''med need''.  I cut & pasted my e-mail string w/Jason in my reply to Chris so he sees my response because he was asking how the ''claim'' was going.
     * Chris wanted me to chg his e-mail address.  I included the link to Patti''s Memb Chg Form in my reply & let him know it must go thru the back office so they can change it in the various component & billing sections of his memb.  I let him know I cannot do that for him either.     - CA

Chris reponded re: colonoscopy.  It was 3-mos ago.  Can he pay & get reim by Zion?  I let him know they allow us 6-mos to sub the ''med need'' & they do reimb, but to remember he is resp for the 1k IUA.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-12 17:57:43', '2023-01-12 18:24:53'),
