In looking over my records, I don''t see any sign of preventative included for these conversion folks without adding the MEC. I don''t see anything special for DPC other than perhaps the lower price bc of DPC. So, it appears she will need to add the MEC to get wellness. Adding it will bring the cost up to $860 from $491.50. It''s likely not worth it! She has a $500 mammogram she already did. If she needs a colonoscopy she might just want to shop around. $368.50x12 is $4422 extra per year to change to DIRECT.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-11 09:42:16', '2023-01-11 09:50:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111509003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032016379', 'Maurine Killough', NULL, '1-11-22 Maurine called late yesterday and I just listened to the vm. She''s in the ER and was for 2 nights. Hoping to leave today. She had some foreign metal substance or object in her system that they had to remove. She just traveled back from Egypt and they think it''s from a metal brush you use on grills. That sounds crazy to me. But, they don''t have the pathology lab back yet today. They did a laproscopy. They removed all of it and she doing much better now. They''ve taken really good care of her. She''s in Mills Peninsula Hospital in Burlingame, CA. She knows to create the Need right away as soon as she has a bill. She was going to start it now, but realizes she will wait until she has a bill. I gave her MPB Concierge Team''s # to call for assistance. She thinks she already knows how to create a need but will call them if she needs any help. She had given the office her MPB.Health card and the Planstin card. I told her to remove the Planstin card bc that will cause problems. She will do that. The QR code is relevant so they can keep that on file. She said she set that up correctly. She was appreciative of my call and will proceed with the Need.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-11 09:37:23', '2023-01-11 09:37:23'),
