  ('zcrm_1579374000111397089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029364085', 'Kristy Tripp', NULL, '1-10-22 After talking with Patti, I sent this to Zion.
Hi Member Care Team,

My client Kristy Tripp contacted Zion about a mammogram she recently completed. Zion''s Team told her the mammogram is not shareable and recommended she adds a MEC to her membership. However, our records show she is on the Worksite DPC plan for our conversion clients who also had immediate sharing. Our understanding is the DPC plan includes access to preventive mammograms and colonoscopies after a 6 month waiting period. She is far beyond the waiting period. Can you please double check her account and make sure the records are accurate and explain why she''s told the mammogram is not shareable?

Thanks!!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-10 17:31:50', '2023-01-10 17:31:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111397081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111961002', 'Philip Kendzior', NULL, '1-10-22 Jennifer and family live in Carbondale, CO. Referred by Rachel Brisson. Jennifer''s a teacher and her ins is paid for by school district but rest of the family costs $1200! There are no chronic health issues. Husband is 53 and he had an old shoulder surgery 20 years ago. They''ll make sure he doesn''t have anything recently in past 24 months. They watched the video which was super helpful. Husband is self-employed. Daughter has glasses and VSP would be helpful. Looking at SECURE $625/$1000 for Feb. 1st start date. She will discuss it with her husband and I will meet with her next week to enroll. She''s also interested in HMA and possibly 10,000 for $140 for dental, vision, medical, etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-10 17:20:39', '2023-01-10 17:21:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111427032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032679122', 'Marty Kirby', NULL, '01.10.2023 Jodi called to confirm they still have coverage, because she was not seeing the December amount contribution withdrawn from her account.
I went into Admin123 and confirmed a payment had be withdrawn on 12/20, and to look for another payment on the 20th of Jan. 
Right before I hung up with Jodi, she shared how the amount I gave her was different from what she is used to seeing.
I went back and checked, and I had viewed the wrong "Kirby".I found the right account and learned, that they are part of the Sedera Conversion pool, but did not complete the conversion.
I called Jodi back, after consulting with Cari for extra guidance. Cari said to possibly consult with Patti, and send Jodi to leaver her a VM. I called Jodi back, explained the account and conversion situation, and letting her know that her account is not active as a result. She shared she thought those emails sent out were just newsletters, so she deleted them. I asked her if she did not hear from her advisor, Sammi, and she said "no" she did not hear from Sammi Bessert. She asked me (for Sammi I learned later) if Sammi was still with MPB. I said yes to her thinking if the name pops up, they are with us. But I learned from Cari that Sammi is NOT active with MPB.
Due to Cari reaching out to Patti earlier for this situation, Cari went ahead and sent Patti the message via teams, just in case Jodi''s VM does not complete. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-10 17:02:48', '2023-01-10 17:38:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111397073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047238273', 'Jennifer Bradfield', NULL, '1-10-22 I left vm and confirmed price and let him know we have to complete change form and find out if he completed Sedera upgrade yet or not. If not, he needs to select Add MEC. Price above is correct. Also let him know we need to make the change by Jan. 15th!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-10 16:58:24', '2023-01-10 16:58:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111397068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014431007', 'Suzanne Cote', NULL, '1-10-22 I left her a vm and let her know most imp is to make her initial and ongoing payment with Cigna ASAP. Let her know other they will cancel and she''ll have no plan for 2023. Also, if did fail to do so, we only have until the 15th to re-enroll. Hopefully she understood my babbling vm to get that done immediately. I also thanked her for sending Carol Prendergast my way. UPDATE I gave her verbal instructions to pay. She did not make an initial payment. Crossing our fingers they will allow her to. I gave her the policy #.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-10 16:53:50', '2023-01-10 17:06:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111427024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097703002', 'Laura Most', NULL, '01.10.2023 Laura called to change her banking information. I confirmed her account and I guided her to the Member Update page to the appropriate Cognito form. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-10 14:56:11', '2023-01-10 14:56:11'),
