I told him that is a direct medical need requirement, given that it is an injury. I confirmed with Cari via teams, and she added to make sure they present themselves as cash-pay patients and request the cash-pay discount, with medical coding. Once they have established the initial visit and the stated invoices, to call the Concierge line back and we will guide them to opening a medical need. 
Charles did say they have not had their welcome call (although it shows that Vanessa completed it in the profile), so I did go ahead and resend the welcome call scheduling email to them. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-01-10 13:31:16', '2023-01-10 13:32:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111419007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083937002', 'Benjamin Lee', NULL, '1-10-2023:  Ora called.  They want to sched Benjamin''s colonoscopy, but are in no hurry.  We disc their receiving a new pdf Planstin card & that will change the req for the providers selected.  Ora''s going to contact us either: when they rec that new card, or will call us around 1/25/2023 if they haven''t rec''d it yet.  If needed we can go over in ntwk providers, but w/colonoscopies it''s far more diff because dr, facility, anesthesiologist all needing to be in ntwk.  We did disc ''prev'' vs ''diagnostic'' should they pull a polyp = no chg for ''prev screening'' / 1k IUA if polyp pulled & goes to a diagnostic procedure involving the healthshare comp.
     - She mentioned Benjamin is having surgery in Feb 2023, but we did not discuss at all.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-10 13:17:25', '2023-01-10 14:20:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111397032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '1-10-22 Rachel''s response to how the membership worked. She''s cancelling bc her husband is getting a family plan at no cost to them!
Hi Wendy,

  Thanks for the quick response and info. I have submitted the form and understand regarding the payment. Always good to ask…Honestly, these benefits have been great to us over the years I would have kept them but my husband’s company has a great plan with no premium so that made the decision easy.

We did use them for our annual visits and a procedure my son had to have done and it was all a great experience. You have been really helpful to us and our industry over the years.

