  ('zcrm_1579374000111222003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104973012', 'Lynne Howard', NULL, '01.09.23@2:24 pm- Lynne called about getting a prescription quote. It was muffled call like when you have a three way call. I could hear well but she complained  that there was an eco o my call.  Not sure who is her advisor since her record reads Current Concepts Corporation.  Lynne is not used to people who speak more than one language. She was polite even though she had a little trouble with my pronunciation of the word "quote" ... she understood code. . I sent her a prescription quote from . Rb.', 'Rosana Bowman', 'Rosana Bowman', '2023-01-09 12:24:49', '2023-01-09 12:24:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111190032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110974002', 'Heather Juby', NULL, 'Spoke to Heather today, welcomed her, and answered some of her questions. She is scheduled to do her welcome call after Feb 1 effective date.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-01-09 12:13:54', '2023-01-09 12:13:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111190027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100532002', 'Rhona Flanagan', NULL, 'Spoke to Rhona, they had a drop in income and qualified for a large subsidy through ACA. Low monthly premium, and very low deductible. Sent CXL form.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-01-09 11:59:58', '2023-01-09 11:59:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111190019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060480020', 'Marian Salley', NULL, '1-8-22 Playing phone tag.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-09 11:40:09', '2023-01-09 11:40:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111190014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012048004', 'Paula Slick', NULL, '1-9-22 Paula called bc she''s been trying desperately to make her pmt to Cigna to effectuate her plan and Cigna finds no record of her plan yet. Her account was changed between Dec. 1st and Dec. 15th. She chose a new plan and had to remove the old one. That worked at the time but she has to be one of the clients in the mess of C4 that didn''t submit correctly to the carrier. She spent many hours on hold with Cigna this morning and her son tried to help her make the payment without success. Her cc was denied even though it has plenty of credit on it. I read to her the email from C4 about those affected by this issue.  They are advised that they will be covered and backdated. But, she thinks she might have broken a rib and needs it checked ASAP. She wants to make sure it''s not going to puncture her lung or anything terrible like that. I coached her to go in a self-pay patient to an independent facility that can do imaging. She will do that and prefers to get it checked and pay the cash price than worry about getting reimbursed since that may take forever. If she needs surgery, I told her to let me know and I''ll submit an Escalation for her in that case. She contemplated changed carriers but I don''t think that will solve the problem since this is a C4 issue all around. She will also call C4 to get her attempts documented and I told her to get a ticket # and to send it to me to keep in her file. This will show proof in case further problems. Also, Paula tried to contact Northwestern Family Medicine in Superior, CO to help her and they say they won''t accept her without insurance. To avoid further problems since she''s already a patient of theirs, she will find a separate independent facility she can go to as self-pay. She also wants to submit a complain to DORA. But, I don''t know that it will matter since C4 is openly working to resolve the problem.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-09 11:36:30', '2023-01-09 11:47:26'),
