  ('zcrm_1579374000110772018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165360', 'Connie Mansour', NULL, '1-3-22 I talked with Connie and they have a $60K taxable retirement fund they are trying to manage unexpectedly that they were forced to liquidate with Vanguard.  So, now she won''t qualify for many of the low income benefits she''s been getting bc they are pushed into this higher tax bracket. If she kept her silver plan it was going to vost $438.06. The Friday Gold plan would be about $285.53. But, the bronze plan with Vision Exam will cost only $1.93 after the applied APTC $1204.38. The tax credit showed as $1340.41 but didn''t use it all with the Bronze plan. It looks like APTC doesn''t apply to the vision exam for some reason. Either way, she will save $3426.36 vs the Gold plan and she gets co-pays instead of co-ins for many items, plus no cost preventative, PCP and mental health visits. So, the best option.
