  ('zcrm_1579374000110778003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000035547415', 'Grant Curatola', NULL, '1-3-2023:  Grant called to cancel &amp; had questions as to whether he has credit left?  I trans him dir to Jeffrey Bursteen, sent Jeffrey a Teams chat too.  He knows to LM for Jeffrey if he doesn''t catch him.  Grant also knows there will be a legal form he will need to sign &amp; Jeffrey will walk him thru the process.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-01-03 12:29:12', '2023-01-03 12:29:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110772013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165360', 'Connie Mansour', NULL, '12-27-22 "Hi Wendy, I hope you had a fun restful Xmas.  We continued with Friday Health but the adjustment from Colo Health Op wasn''t updated so we got billed full rate for January 2023.  I have updated our financials on the website form.  Just waiting for updated bill. Let me know if this is correct way to proceed.  Thank you for your help and hope to see you soon."
Connie

My response "Hi Connie!

Nice to hear from you. I just called Connect for Health CO and we can''t update your income for Jan. 1st now otherwise they will cancel your current plan which you don''t want to do. We can push through the new income amount after Jan. 1st and before Jan. 15th. I also don''t see any Advanced Premium Tax Credit for Jan. This is strange. But, if we mess with it you''ll be cancelled since you missed the deadline to make changes for Jan. 1st. UGH! You will receive tax credit when you file your taxes for 2023. Can you swing it for the one month?  Your tax credit for Feb. onward will be $1340.41 as long as we select the plan before Jan. 15th!  Let me know your thoughts.

Best wishes and Happy Holidays,', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-03 12:28:47', '2023-01-03 12:28:47'),
