Sedera &amp; Redirect cancelled - 12/23  Member refunded 12/27', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-23 08:28:30', '2022-12-27 08:42:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110124008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106964002', 'Cynthia Unger', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-12-23 08:25:57', '2022-12-23 08:25:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110105014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108411002', 'Andrew Buschbacher', NULL, 'Asked member to reschedule his welcome call due to MPB being closed for the New Year holiday. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-12-23 08:05:51', '2022-12-23 08:05:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110105009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037141080', 'James Ashford', NULL, 'James called in before I could get to his question on SalesIQ. We got him all set with his CirrusMD account so he can hopefully feel better before Christmas. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-12-23 07:46:45', '2022-12-23 07:46:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110102004', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037141080', 'James Ashford', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Healthcare Advisor', 'Visit ID : 2629 Question : What service replaces teledoc', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2022-12-23 07:41:01', '2022-12-23 07:41:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110088002', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037141080', 'James Ashford', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Leonardo Moraes', 'Visit ID : 2628 Question : What app replaced Teledoc. Need to use the service this morning', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2022-12-23 07:40:24', '2022-12-23 07:40:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110124003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109380026', 'Caesare Sanchez', NULL, 'Spoke to member will reschedule online the welcome call after start date of January 1, 2023. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-12-23 07:35:06', '2022-12-23 07:35:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110112003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108862002', 'Mark Witt', NULL, 'Member submitted PU form I will update in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-23 07:29:58', '2022-12-23 07:29:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110110003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081238002', 'Joseph Scaturro', NULL, 'Jennifer forwarded the email from this member, indicating he would like to cancel his plan by Jan 1,2023.
I left a message on his voicemail to call me back.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-12-23 07:19:38', '2022-12-23 07:19:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110060063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094922002', 'Lindsey Frick', NULL, '12-22-2022:  Lindsey got ahold of the financial help department and she''s 100% covered so she''s not going to need to start a need for her ER visit.  Cleveland Clinic let her know they''ll pay for whatever she need thru 3/2023(?) & I told her to confirm on ea item prior to treatment, but why not take advantage of that.
     - She was ok w/$2500, but when we disc she could be resp for up to 3 IUAs a year, she may discuss the price diff w/her aunt = her advisor: Sally Thomsen.
     - She also wanted to know about adding ''prev care'' & I let her know beg 1/1/23, the ntwk will no longer be utilized & explained how it will be & that her aunt may not even know that yet, since I don''t think they''ve announced it to the field yet.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-22 18:44:11', '2022-12-23 15:39:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110060055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005667255', 'Kathleen Kronz', NULL, '12-22-2022:  Kathleen is a very distracted and challenging personality.  Nice enough, but she doesn''t always let you finish & struggles to focus since she''s paying at Costco, or...
     - Her first concern was getting everything done before the end-of-the year.  (Note: there are all of 6 possible business days this year & she doesn''t even have doctor relationships!)  We went over the change in ''prev care'' starting 1/1/2023 = no ntwk req''d & I explained it will open up to doctors that are willing to work out pricing w/Planstin & are willing to bill for the pt.  Then she was worried because she thought she was missing out on things she should have had this yr.  I explained, that it''s not calendar year.  That if she had something they allow once a year, it''s more the 13th month she''d be elig again.  That seemed to help.
     - She complained about not understanding all of the components.  I sent her a copy of her post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail & explained that it is a great resource.  She wanted to find a new doc, so I explained & highlighted the ''HCBB'' section.
     - We went over how IUAs work: Issue Spec, not annual w/an ongoing need, 3/yr, 4th & beyond, etc.
     - Wanted to do a Cologuard Test, so we discussed the disadvantage if it comes out positive = lots of false positives, so the doctor wants to do a screening colonoscopy, but the ''prev care'' only pays for one or the other, not both.  Went over the ''MEC'' section that is in the post ''Welcome Call'' section & how she has a link there to the healthcare.gov site & list of ''prev care'' included.  IF she wants further specifics, we can always turn to the TPA for detailed ans.  Let her know the one lab we are seeing consistently pd for is the lipid panel.
     I think by the time we got done, she was in a much better place & understood that she''s not in the crazy rush she thought she was.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-22 18:28:13', '2022-12-22 18:33:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110060050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109087002', 'Michelle McCartney', NULL, '12-22-2022:  Michelle called to cancel (her eff date isn''t until 1/1/23, but she''s decided to go the traditional ins route w/sub.  I trans her to Jeffrey Burnsteen''s line &amp; didn''t get this documented prior to his calling her.  Therefore, I did not send him a Teams chat.  He''s already on it.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-22 18:14:53', '2022-12-22 18:14:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110060045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075520001', 'Scott Totten', NULL, '12-22-2022:  Deborah called, Scott''s wife, Scott ended up in the ER.   They were able to get his afib under control and released him, so at least he was not admitted to the hosp.
     - He was given an RX for Eliquis 5mg, taking 1 tab twice a day.  I quoted locally and the RX right next door to where he works has one of the lowest prices:  Disc Drug Mart = $518.32.  The pharmacy had already gotten them that price on GoodRX, so I did not send them a coupon.  Since they have the ER need & the exp for this RX is > $500/mo, I told them to save the RX receipt to sub on the need, but there is no guarantee they will inclue the RX in the ''med need'', it''s just worth trying.
     - The mfg site for RX asst on Eliquis = Bristol Meyer Squibb Pt Asst Foundation.  Ph #: 1-800-736-1611.  general site = www.bmspaf.org.  Tamara told me a household of 2 people, making < $54,930 can sub an appl (pt portion, md port, & proof of inc via tax ret) for = free RX assistance.  I sent all the info, site, ph #, downloaded appl to the e-mail in this file.
     - Reid also gave me a quote & I passed that info along = Eliquis 5mg x 168tabs $211.75 + $9.95 shipping & that it''s a 4-week delivery so we''d need to hop on this.
     - They have nothing to sub with the ''med need'', so Deborah knows we need to walk thru sub the ''med need'' right away so they can get the approval process started.  She''s going to connect with the ER billing office to see if they have their ''cash-pay'' price yet.  Note: they went to Cleveland Clinic that is notorious for issues w/''cash-pay'' patients.
     The soonest Scott could get an appt w/his cardiologist = Feb...     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-22 17:06:48', '2022-12-22 17:06:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110084003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504120', 'William Madsen', NULL, '12-22-22 Bill was shocked to see his new bill at $800+ a month from $550. He was pissed to say the least. I don''t see the email from MPB sent to him. After going over the price choices with new IUA''s, he''s choosing CARE+ instead. They haven''t been making use of the wellness visits and he has an HSA but hasn''t been funding it. So, he''ll go with CARE+ for this year at $1000/$520. This will keep his cost down and still very good benefits.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-22 15:56:14', '2022-12-22 15:56:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110075026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108411002', 'Andrew Buschbacher', NULL, '12.22.2022 Andrew called to address an email he received about a declined payment.
I asked him if he thinks he needs to make any changes to his payment process, he responded "possibly".
I guided him to the change form on Member Portals and Updates, where he completed the form while I was on-line with him.
I checked the payment change forms on Cognito, and I confirmed it was there. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2022-12-22 15:18:40', '2022-12-22 15:32:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110075021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504120', 'William Madsen', NULL, '12.22.2022 Bill called to understand why Sedera''s increased the amount on his bill.
I explained that Sedera is going through changes and has converted platforms, and the members are required to complete and sign some papers. 
He asked why would that increase his bill, but I needed to get back to him on that question after I investigate it with my trainer. I did shed light on that I learned that when the members are calling Sedera directly to make these changes/conversions, they Sedera is adding elements/services onto their bill that they already have through MPB. Therefore, it is important that they complete the change process with their advisor. 
Bill was understanding, I gave him Wendy''s number and I direct transferred him. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2022-12-22 15:11:30', '2022-12-22 15:26:51'),
