  ('zcrm_1579374000109773058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123724002', 'Thomas, Sr. Mastroianni', NULL, 'Tom is in philly pa, he''s got family and kids and is 1099, he is currently with samaritan and wants to switch. we will reconvene friday, also update him on potential enrollment date.', 'Tony Manzanarez', 'Tony Manzanarez', '2022-12-20 18:02:08', '2022-12-20 18:02:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109798026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088967001', 'Kristen Victor', NULL, '12.20.2022 Kristen called looking for an OBGYN and Colonoscopy in network doctors.
I shared about the change of network need starting January 2023, and if she''s not in a hurry, to go ahead and plan her appointments for after that.
Kristen said her appts are for February and March. She asked to explain the change and I said she would be able to see the doctor of her choosing. Except she needs to make sure they are willing to communicate with Planstin to collaborate pricing.
Because she was worried about her doctor still not being in "network" and maybe not wanting to reach out to Planstin, I decided to pull Cari in for further guidance for Kristen and additional coaching for me.
Cari further explained how to communicate with the providers in order to process her bills, and that she is no longer bound to a network, as long as all providers involved will acccept payment. 
Kristen continued to request a recommendation for the stated above, and Cari proceeded to show her to use Healthcare BlueBook. I emailed her the link to start with.
Cari gave her the log-in information and set up to start using the site, and  to type ONLY ''COLO'' to choose Gastroenterology. 
Cari proceeded to explain how HCBB works and how Kristen can use it to her benefit in the future. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2022-12-20 17:01:37', '2022-12-23 11:39:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109778132', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109354202', 'Louis Romero', NULL, '12-20-22 Louis let me know his income changed from $107K to $38,584 bc both jobs laid him off. This happened in Sept 23rd and he applied for unemployment starting Oct. 1st. His new chosen plan is RMHP Colorado Doctors Plan Silver $4,500 ($0 Virtual Urgent Care + $0 Primary Care Visits, $3 T2 Preferred Rx Copay) Silver/HMO $2,357.91, APTC $2,006.81 and his cost is $351.10.  He was shocked to see his plan cost had increased from $801 to $1100 for unknown reasons. So, he called to find out. Once learning of his income change, I updated his account to show his new income for 2022 and 2023.  The Gold plan no longer made sense. He chose the plan above and was thrilled!  This will help him tremendously while he gets back onto his feet with a new job. He will call C4 now to request a Jan. 1st start date, if possible as well. If not, he''ll pay the $1100 for one month. I also cancelled his dental per his request but it''s still showing on his enrollments. I will cancel again.
UPDATE- He''s talking to C4 now and will ask them to cancel his dental plan for 2023. He said it''s worthless. They don''t cover much.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-20 16:19:44', '2022-12-20 16:26:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109778127', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044725092', 'Mark Garcia', NULL, '12-20-22 Mark is deciding to cancel PDHC and enrolling in SECURE $1000/$325. I waived the $100 Admin Fee. He grilled me on the pricing and changes with Sedera first and everything I said was in alignment with the person he spoke with at Sedera. His past injuries from his bike accident are are healed and no problems. His only concern was his cholesterol which I read and he read the section of the newest Sharing Guidelines that states it''s exempt assuming no problems in the past 12 months. We will make sure to cancel PDHC next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-20 15:39:10', '2022-12-20 15:39:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109798018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075132121', 'Inga Hughes', NULL, '12.20.2022 Inga called to learn how to open a medical need for a procedure she had done (maybe yesterday) on her gums. 
I proceeded to gather more information via teams with Cari, given that we do not cover dental.
With Cari''s guidance, I was able to ask Inga detailed questions to identify if it is shareable.
Inga had an evaluation on her gums back in 4/2022, which goes past the 6 month deadline with Zion.
I offered to guide her to open a medical need anyways to start a communication with Zion, with Cari''s coaching to have her ask Zion about the "special fund", should they decline her need request.
I brought Cari in on the call to help solidify the above to Inga and explain further that her gum disease surgery would not be considered shareable with Zion. ...
gave our email to forward what she sent to Zion: info@mympb.com', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2022-12-20 15:19:37', '2022-12-20 16:38:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109778122', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095912017', 'Alicia Hutchens', NULL, '12-20-22 I talked with Mara and she helped me recognize the downfalls if Alicia chooses to cancel her NLG plan at $400K death benefit. She will lose all of her Living Benefits that will NOT be offered in any group life ins policy. If she gets sick and uses all of the cash value in her company policy and is still sick, she may become un-insurable. One client had this happen. She got cancer, used up her cash value, couldn''t work, got laid off, went onto Cobra for 18 months. Then after all of that she was un-insurable without a job and still fighting cancer with mounting bills and a child to support. I was disastrous. Also, she will lose her ability to try holistic or experimental treatments that could potentially save her life. Finally most term life plans through work are $250K or less. So, she will be even further exposing herself to troubles, if something bad happens. 
I left her a vm just now to explain this to her before she chooses to cancel NLG.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-20 15:15:39', '2022-12-20 15:15:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109710314', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028584125', 'Brian Schiller', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation from as he is getting Employer Benefits.  I will cancel', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-20 14:56:19', '2022-12-20 15:00:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109724037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063804100', 'Roger Gaudreau', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Leonardo Moraes', 'Visit ID : 2618 Question : We currently have MPowering Secure Care $615.00 Member + Family - $2500 IUA and we are considering removing our son. Can you tell me what a the difference in monhtly fee would be?', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2022-12-20 14:51:03', '2022-12-20 14:51:03'),
