  ('zcrm_1579374000109490023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036377153', 'William Moomaw', NULL, '12-16-22 Mat is enrolling in CARE+ now after looking at how bad the traditional ins options are. He reviewed everything I sent and he''s choosing $2500/$185 and I waived the $100 since he''s already been a member. He just cancelled his PDHC bc the price increased so much for him. He''s healthy, no issues and no preventative needs. His new account will be under Mat instead of William.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-16 12:09:05', '2022-12-16 12:11:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109473119', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058401239', 'emmett murphy', NULL, 'Member submitted Change request to add spouse &amp; children to membership eff 1/1/23 I will update &amp; notify Planstin', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-16 12:07:09', '2022-12-16 12:07:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109500003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000040737005', 'Bernard Mumford', NULL, 'I spoke to Bernard, nice guy. I explained the change in the Sedera platform and the requirement to do the re-enrollment. His concern was that his DPC is retiring. However, he understandss he will have ot pay for visits out of pocket, but it will balance out because he will no longer have to cover the monthly fee to the doctor. I gave him all my direct  contact info.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-12-16 11:57:34', '2022-12-16 11:57:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109480018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000020603201', 'Kamaljeet Singh', NULL, '12-16-2022:  Kamaljeet called re: Sedera conversion.  I let him know his advisor, Kevin Michaels is the one who can help him thru the process.  In case Kevin needs help, I mentioned Kevin can reach out to Wendy.  I let him know Sedera is just making chgs for compliance.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-16 11:55:00', '2022-12-16 11:55:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109490018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165343', 'Renee Athay', NULL, '12-16-22 Renee explained to me her entire situation with Zion. She hadn''t seen a dermatologist for 15 years and decided to go in April. They found 7 spots and 5 needed to be addressed. She communicated with Zion with tons of back and forth in April and May to provide what they wanted which was different documentation. She did her best until they wanted her to separate out each Need, ie. each spot as a new Need. She had no idea how to do that since it was happening in the same visits. She gave up and then paid the cash price and it has been about $11K and 5 different skin spots that needed biopsies and such. I explained the 6 month time frame but I''m hoping she within the window since she began communications with Zion in April and continued to do so until June or so, when she had to just pay cash before it hit her credit score for non-payment.  I connected her with Jennifer who will reach out to her contact at Zion to work towards next steps to resolve this. Also Renee turns 65 in Feb. She''s trying to balance signing up for Medicare with getting reimbursed by Zion. She doesn''t want to damage the process with Zion if she cancelled. She knows it safest to keep her account opened while they work through the process to reimburse her. She was incredibly grateful for my help over the years!  She couldn''t have been nicer, truly. I''m crossing my fingers Zion will honor at least some of the bills she submits and reimburses her. She also told me the house her family grew up in and her father built in Paragon Estates off S. Boulder burnt to the ground. They haven''t lived in it for a long time, but it was still utterly gone.  She recognizes how quickly life can change and nobody is immune to the devastation.  If she gets refunded from Zion she''s planning to give it to some charities. She was super fortunate to have money from the sale of a property to pay for her medical bills. If it happened before, she never would have been able to pay the bills when Zion was dragging their feet. I''m hoping they won''t dock her on the 6 month time limit. He last conversation with Zion was June 21st. I don''t know how much of the costs were from prior and how many within these past 6 months. Crossing my fingers for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-16 11:38:23', '2022-12-16 21:27:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109473114', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993367', 'Mike Santistevan', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to update address and remove son from membership eff 1/1/23.  I will notify Sedera of these changes.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-16 11:36:26', '2022-12-16 11:36:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109490013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043608546', 'Paige Kaufmann', NULL, '12-16-22 Paige decided to keep their price and IUA as is. I started to explain SECURE but she stopped me and let me know all 4 family members use the chiro services 1x per month. So, any monthly savings would be lost if they give up Redirect. So, she''s happy to pay the higher rate. The other IUA''s were barely any savings. She will leave it all alone and complete the upgrade asap. I sent her the code since she had already started the process and let her know not to add anything to the membership.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-16 11:31:32', '2022-12-16 11:31:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109490008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109491027', 'Allison McFee', NULL, '12-16-22 Allie is enrolling in CARE+ $1000/$240, no pre-x, no meds and moves around a ton! She will be traveling again as of Dec 21. She''ll do her Welcome Call upon return in the new year. That works well for her. She is starting to wrap her head around how it works and is thankful that she''s protected while abroad as well. She also realizes it would take a lot to exceed the IUA when abroad.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-16 11:25:07', '2022-12-16 11:25:07'),
