  ('zcrm_1579374000109358086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081869008', 'Frederick Koen', NULL, '12-14-22 Tina has been very eager to get this done. She sent me the proposal sent by Cesar at Zion. It''s saved in her file. The quote was for $1894 which included medical, dental, vision, accident and mental health. They added some monthly $10 fee for Admin plus about $300 set up fees. I sent her my best quote with SECURE and HMA at $1745 with a $200 1x enrollment fee and no annual fees or other Admin fees. Cesar has also mentioned doing a 125 Cafeteria Plan for tax benefits. I let her know she will have the HSA tax benefits as well as a portion of the membership is tax ded. In this case it''s $105x3= $315 of the $1745. But, also saving $1904-$1745 = $159 per month.  I don''t believe she can have the MCS as pre-tax! John and Michele are ready to create her customized site and List Bill, etc. I''ve asked to meet with her at 2:00 tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-14 20:35:57', '2022-12-14 20:35:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109358075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109354142', 'Angela Coy', NULL, '12-14-22 See notes from her other cloned account!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-14 20:21:13', '2022-12-14 20:21:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109358067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077830004', 'Angela Coy', NULL, '12-14-22 Angela, Don Coy (her fahter) and I discussed her options and she chose Cigna Connect Colorado Option Silver
Silver/EPO $322.92, 	APTC $252.96. Her annualized income for 2022 was about $24K. She''s changing jobs so her income for 2023 is uncertain. So, we put it at $24K as the best guess. They didn''t want Medicaid so she has more choices in docs and a good plan. She also didn''t fully understand how to use CARE+. She had called Zion at some point when she needed urgent care (I think that''s what she said). Virtual Healthcare would have solved the problem but they simply told her it wouldn''t be shareable.  She had about 6 different appointments for 6 different issues and felt like her plan didn''t cover anything. The problem is her father tries to take care of everything for her, so she didn''t even have CirrusMD on her phone. All that said, at $24K income, she will only have to pay $69.96 for a plan with a $100 Ded and $1000 MOP. So, she will be happier with this while she''s not earning much. However, she will keep her account opened until she figures out if  she can get reimbursed for her Need since it was in Sept. She will look at her bills to see if they exceeded $1000 and call the MPB Concierge Team.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-14 20:17:09', '2022-12-14 20:17:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109358059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069438001', 'Beth Blacker', NULL, '12-14-22 To Beth - I called and spoke with Raquel at C4HCO just now. She confirmed the APTC amount of $446.53 and your cost at $449.71. She and I agree to leave your account alone. The outbound EDI transactions has already been sent to the carrier with that exact information. She made very specific notes on your account in case there''s any trouble down the road. That''s what they should honor. Your ticket # is 221214-004323 in case you need it. This is the documentation showing the above. 

I sent her a screen shot via email with the date stamp in the lower right as well.

I thought we changed income to $61740 but it''s showing as $66740.  Either way, we didn''t re-enroll. We left it alone since her income is very uncertain.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-14 20:03:29', '2022-12-14 20:08:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109379040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099565002', 'Dennis Flannigan', NULL, '12-12-2022:  Dennis called.  He was notified by CVS in Safeway(?) that they randomly refillis his RXs at the Aurora store, rather than the Littleton store where he got them before.  He wanted to know why we were making him go so far.  I assured him we do not touch your prescriptions, we just find the best pricing for you, but you decide where to get them.  He said when he got there they had a 60-day supply ready, but the price was drastically higher then it had been before, so they told him to wait 30-minutes & they''d go to a 30-day supply, which t wasurned out to be even more expensive the the 60-ds!  By now he''s totally angry.  
     He says when he was signing up for this healthcare, his advisor Christine Corsini had looked & told him his RXs are covered.  I asked what card he''d presented & he said he hadn''t given them any card.  He used to be on BCBS, where the 30ds for the 2 RXs was ~$20.  Who knows where they got the info... Or did he use an OptumRX card & forgot he''d given it to them?
     I priced up his 2 RXs & found Cost+ was the least exp manner to get these by $10, even with s&h.  He''s in no hurry, so we walked thru their site together to get him ready to order via their srvc.  He wants to just reorder easily, so this may be a good option.  Here are the items we priced:
     - Valsartan 320mg, #90 (takes 1 daily) = $26.90 w/s&h thru Cost+
     - Metoprolol Succinate ER 25mg, #90 (takes 1 a day) = $10.70 w/s&h thru Cost+     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-14 18:33:43', '2022-12-14 18:33:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000109379035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082410002', 'Nicholas Burdick', NULL, '12-13-2022:  We were able to get Nicholas an OptumRX manual reimb form for his kids'' immunizations.  I e-mailed it to him and let him know I sent it.
