  ('zcrm_1579374000108515003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091292', 'Carl Cheetham', NULL, '12.05.22:  Recvd. an email from Carl.  He''s thinking the DIRECT plan would be the best option for him and his children.  He asked if there are any networks to deal with in the plan.  I responded that there are no networks and I agree this plan is the best option for his current needs.  I asked him to confirm this is the plan he wants and gave him the next 3 steps to changing his plan from SECURE to DIRECT.
Carl emailed he has decided to take DIRECT for himself and his children and asked me to call him whenever I''m available to move ahead with the cancellation and enrollment process. I responded I can call him this afternoon at 3 p.m. if that works for him.
Emailed Carl that he can use the Member Change Form (which I included) to remove his wife, Melissa, from his plan as well as change his plan from SECURE to DIRECT. Said I would call him at 2:30 p.m. to guide him in filling out this form.
Called and spoke w/Carl.  Further explained the DIRECT plan and how the Zion preventive care program works (w/caps on each of the services).  I also explained he will receive an email from Patti with his login and password and instructions to follow in resigning the membership document, which also gives old and new price.  I relayed to Carl that Patti told me if Carl moves from SECURE to DIRECT, he will not be able to switch back for one year from start date of new plan.
Carl had already completed and submitted the Member/Plan Change form.  I notified him of the new services we have and the new MPB app that will allow him to access all of our services from one place.  He was very happy with this.  I also strongly recommended he schedule a new Welcome Call to learn more about accessing his DIRECT plan.
I emailed Carl to summarize our call.  
I notified Jeffrey in Teams that Carl will not be cancelling his plan but changed his plan.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2022-12-05 11:28:12', '2022-12-05 13:11:25'),
