  ('zcrm_1579374000108426003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084517001', 'Kyle King', NULL, '12/3/2022:  Kyle let me know, Zion has declined her jaw bone graph as ''Dental'' and she''s really feeling like she''s paying all this money for nothing.  We went back to basics & disc what the MPB Pkg she purch includes & does not.  How the diff comp are not linked, what ea does, & how the Conc Line or I can try to guide her:
     - Planstin = Prev Only (there are almost no in ntwk docs near here), so she feels like the ''prev'' is worthless.  I let her know we are working on the RBP but this isn''t guaranteed.  She will touch base w/me in Jan.
     - Re: Dental issue - we went over several dental policy options, HMA, HSA, etc.  I''m sending her the info on the dental & HMA, but doesn''t feel like she makes enough $ to have opened an HSA.
     - We also disc sending an appeal letter to Zion to see if they have any funds in the spec fund that she might be able to use.  She seemed to think this was worthless, yet I sugg it couldn''t hurt.  Even if they just throw in a little money.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-03 22:49:26', '2022-12-03 22:49:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108405114', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088734001', 'Matthew Larson', NULL, '12-2-2022:  Matt called to work on getting his son''s ''med need'' going.  It sounds like his son''s ins from his missionary work expires on 12/20/2022.  
     - Chemo begins on 12/15/2022, so they will have help w/this round.
     - He''s going to gather the dates everything has happened, get the documents into pdf or on his comp as pict, then will call us for guidance.  The other ins pays for everything while it''s in effect.  No copays.  No ded.  But, starting the ''med need'' now will help get things going for expenses past 12/20/22 when his other ins expires.
     - Matt sounded much better today and seemed grateful for the guidance.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-02 17:36:49', '2022-12-02 17:36:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108405100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075132226', 'Maria Borden', NULL, '12-2-2022:  Maria had a ''prev'' colonoscopy, but it moved to diagnostic.  We talked about sub a ''med need'' &amp; how she''ll be resp for the $1k IUA, but then the healthsharing should help from there.  She''s going to call back when she has her computer so we can show her how to sub the ''med need'', what to upload, what to exp, etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-02 17:20:01', '2022-12-02 17:29:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108405095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081509011', 'Tammy Goen', NULL, '12-2-2022:  Tammy called.
     - She orig had a SECURE memb, but ntwk docs in her area for Planstin were not working for her, so she went to Care+ & gave up the HSA elig.  
        She''s been so impressed w/MPB, she''d like to go back to the SECURE Plan starting 1/1/2023.  I helped her find the ''memb chg form'' so she can submit the req because she wants to supp MPB & be qual for the HSA again.
        I let her know we are trying to get rid of the req''d ntwk on Planstin, but no guarantee & no exact timeline.  She will keep watching the Newsletters & may call next year to see if we have any news.
     -  I think Tammy also asked about colonoscopy info, but the calls were too many, too fast.  My doc above is accurate, but I cannot be sure of everything else.
     - Tammy''s so thrilled w/her MPB Plan & is following our newsletter, so I asked if she''d be open to submitting a video for the newsletter.  She seemed intrigued, but said she''ll think about it.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-02 17:18:31', '2022-12-02 18:01:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108425003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091292', 'Carl Cheetham', NULL, '12.2.22:  Jeffrey call me and said Carl Cheetham called wanting to cancel.  Jeff asked if I want to handle it or if I wanted him to handle it.  I told him I would do it. Jeff asked that if I had difficulty with Carl and couldn''t get him to stay, to let Jeff know and he would take a crack at it to which I agreed.
Called and spoke w/Carl. Said his wife got BCBS insurance w/her co. and they''re covering 75% of the cost.  I explained he needs to calculate if there would be any cost for the entire family to be covered as well as what the deductible and co-pays, etc. are.  I, then, informed him of some changes that have just occurred (Direct plan) and the PHCS to RBP-based plans to come. His one complaint was he had no providers where he lives for preventive care.  I gave him pricing for the Direct plan for M&F and M&C.  He then asked what the price would be for MO, which I gave him.  I told him I would email him my website link so he can review the plan information over the weekend and will get back with him next week to further discuss his needs. Sent the link this evening.  Messaged Jeffrey to let him know I will be following up with Carl.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2022-12-02 15:27:53', '2022-12-02 16:09:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108394028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091292', 'Carl Cheetham', NULL, 'Carl called my direct line and left me a voicemail indicating he wants to cancel. I looked him up and he is Joan Phelp''s member. I called Joan to tell her that Carl wants to cancel, so she could contact him and try to save him. I asked Joan to follow up with me on the status after she speaks with him.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-12-02 15:23:49', '2022-12-02 15:23:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108405090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089447002', 'Rebecca Gradler', NULL, '12-2-2022:  Rebecca called.  She had a ton of questions:
     - She''s frustrated because she''s looking at diff ins and trying to get questions answered, but her advisor has been difficult to get called back from messages she''s left.  I told her I could probably help until he can call them.
     - She''s looking at a plan for just her & her husb that will be 1k/mo & have ~ 14k ded for the two of them.  She''s still struggling to understand the diff between IUA & ded, but had good questions and I think will eventually understand.  We went over this in detail again.  =3 IUAs/memb/yr, not per person, etc.  Went over issue spec & gave examples, etc...
      I sugg several options:
         1) If they are looking at that amount of prem (1k) & that high a ded (14k+), they could pay $915 a mo w/MPB, & go to a 1k IUA.  We talked about how that would save them money w/even 1 single issue in the year.  Pay an extra $2700 over the year, but issues would be shareable at the 1k level.  5000 -1000 = 4000 -2700 = save $1300 w/even one incident. 
         2) She had questions about prev care, derm appts, etc.  Said she isn''t sub anything because she doesn''t think they are cov.  We talked about HSA funds can help here OR I sugg she tt her advisor Michael Montes re: an HMA & briefly described how it is completely diff than the HSA, but would allow them to keep their HSA for retirement and still have a way to get more bang for their buck (totally diff, not your money, only available if you continue to pay, gave 10k level usage example).  With 4 family members, this did intrigue her.  She''s going to try Michael again.
     - She asked about comp & contrasting comp to the ACA plan.  I told her I could help her see how ours works, but am not lic in SC to make sugg, etc, on the ACA plan.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-02 15:17:55', '2022-12-02 17:50:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108419048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037657007', 'Mary Evans', NULL, '12-2-22 Mary EF will go up to $1187.28 or switch to SECURE for $915 EF. Only health thing that happened was Auggie was beaten up in Boulder with $21K expenses. But, he''s 100% good now, no further problems.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-02 15:16:50', '2022-12-02 15:16:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108419043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061092044', 'Charles Kinne', NULL, '12-2-22 Charlie suggested I put in come at $40K. He will get answers about Linda''s Medicare cost for Part A or if it''s free. He wants Delta Dental plans that are not on C4, but direct to Delta Dental per his email. I will send those once I complete the medical part first. He will only be on C4 for next few months until he turns 65 as well. See email to proceed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-02 14:59:48', '2022-12-02 14:59:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108419038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075132226', 'Maria Borden', NULL, '12-2-22 Maria called to ask about her preventative colonoscopy and how to handle it. She didn''t realize she should show her Planstin card. So, she paid cash as follows: $150 deposit, $750 procedure, $565 for sedation and removal of polyps, plus fee for biopsy to total $1825.  I let her know it sounds like the polyp removal/biopsy part might be considered diagnostic and the rest preventative. But, it will be best to get guidance from the MPB Concierge Team since she paid cash already and it''s a reasonable price. It will be easiest if Planstin/Zion can reimburse her, but I have no idea. She was super appreciative and will call Concierge next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-02 14:47:13', '2022-12-02 14:47:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108419033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073598040', 'Jennifer Hushka', NULL, '12-2-22 Jennifer and Gregg are now enrolled in Anthem Colorado Option Gold Pathway Std
