  ('zcrm_1579374000108419003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109371027', 'Karen Faydenko', NULL, '12-2-22 Karen is 53 and husband, Jim is 58. They are on Bright Health now at $980.15 with an APTC. They have a broker for that part. They are both non-smokers, healthy. She takes menopause meds which is generic Prozac. Husband takes blood pressure, cholesterol and possible blood thinner meds. I let her know of the exemptions for high blood pressure and cholesterol if they are well managed and no hospital visits in past 24 months. But, she will find out about the blood thinner meds since that''s not exempt. He also had multiple surgeries in 2020. He had 2 back surgeries and a hip replacement. Hip is doing well! Back is great but sees chiro on occasion. They will check his records and decide if they are comfortable or not with knowing they would have to pay 100% year one.   He''s playing golf and hitting longer than ever.  Live in Morrison, CO. They do their annual wellness visits and Karen has a business, so she''s self-employed. She knows of both deadlines Dec. 15th for ins and Dec. 20th for MCS. I''ll send her the email and she''s hoping to decide today before she leaves for MI. If not, she''ll deal with it while there. Her mother in law is having issues, hence the trip.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-12-02 09:49:38', '2022-12-15 14:52:12'),
