  ('zcrm_1579374000108372008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109496019', 'Bruce Schanstra', NULL, 'we have a call scheduled for tommorow mornining', 'Tony Manzanarez', 'Tony Manzanarez', '2022-12-01 08:13:41', '2022-12-01 08:13:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108367008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084832001', 'Gail Cole', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to change IUA back to $1000.  However she cannot do that as she increase it eff 10/1.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-01 08:13:01', '2022-12-01 08:13:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108372003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109496019', 'Bruce Schanstra', NULL, 'I spoke with Bruce today and he let me know that he currently pay 2495 a month and is looking to start a dpc arrangement with a company called go forward. He is on united but wants to switch over to our SECURE plan. He said he thinks its a done deal if his wife likes the plan and said if his daughters doctors are on network it''s guarenteed he will buy.', 'Tony Manzanarez', 'Tony Manzanarez', '2022-12-01 08:11:48', '2022-12-01 08:11:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108367003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571200', 'Dalton Snook', NULL, 'Member submitted Change Form to increase IUA to $5000 eff 1/1/23.  I will notify Planstin &amp; add new plan in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-01 08:01:26', '2022-12-01 08:01:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108337003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442408', 'Jacquelynn Mariest', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-12-01 07:35:48', '2022-12-01 07:35:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108300036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061045043', 'Kurt Benfield', NULL, 'Member submitted change form to change IUA from $1000 to $5000 eff 1/1/23.  I will notify Planstin &amp; change in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-12-01 07:23:33', '2022-12-01 07:23:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108300031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054286167', 'Catherine McGee', NULL, '11-30-2022:  Catherine called.  She started her ''med need'' &amp; saw what the new surgeon wrote in her records.  In hindsight, she realizes it was her comm that was an issue.  We wrote a letter that included her description to me before she came to Zion.  She has more questions.  I asked her to call me on the concierge line.  She seems to be confused about how pre-x works.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-12-01 03:55:56', '2022-12-01 03:55:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108306003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044118411', 'Nathalie Joly', NULL, '11-30-22 I helped talk her through the conversion process and gave her the new price including the admin fee. She''s fine with everything and nice as always. She''ll call me later about the ERC as well when the dust settles.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-30 23:07:27', '2022-11-30 23:07:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108305018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108399027', 'Doris Medina', NULL, '11-30-22 I went ahead and selected the mid range plan to make sure you are protected for the month of Dec. Today is the deadline.

Here''s what I selected for you: Anthem Bronze Mountain Enhanced X HMO 6000
Bronze/HMO	$1,526.52, APTC $1,252.40

Your cost is $274.12. If you choose to keep this same plan for 2023, your new monthly cost will be $93.34. But, you''re welcome to choose something else of course. You MUST call Anthem in 7-10 business days to make your initial payment for the month of Dec. 2022 to make it effective.  You also need to send me your proof of loss of insurance on 11/30/22. I will upload it to your account to show proof of your special enrollment.

Let''s talk again on Thursday and iron out the final details.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-30 22:38:06', '2022-11-30 22:38:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108305013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108303013', 'Megan Lewis', NULL, '11-30-22 She had troubles enrolling on her own. So, I had to complete it for her to meet the deadline for a Dec. 1st effective date. Here''s what I did and explained to her:
Hi Megan,

OK, I was able to enroll you in a plan for 2022 and 2023. I chose the most similar plan for 2022 as the Cigna plan you want for 2023.

Bright Health Bronze $0 Deductible
Bronze/EPO	$289.58 APTC $128.64


So, your cost for December will be $160.94 for the Bright Health $0 Ded plan. You MUST call the 855-827-4448 number in 7-10 business days to set up your payment for December. 

Then for 2023, I was able to select the following: 
Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0  Bronze/EPO	$351.18	APTC $158.01

Your monthly cost for Jan. 2023 is $193.17. You MUST call 1-877-900-1237 to set up your initial payment and ongoing payments for 2023. You need to do this after 7-10 business days as well. Make sure you follow through or your plans won''t become effective.

Please let me know if you are good with everything! I know you didn''t want to be without insurance for December. So, you will be protected once you make your payments.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-30 22:14:09', '2022-11-30 22:14:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108300023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062380018', 'Daniel Cardoza', NULL, '11-30-2022:  Daniel called - he was in the hosp &amp; wanted to find out what he''ll need to sub a ''med need''.  He wants to call back tomorrow to have us walk him thru the process.  By then, he''ll have everything ready to upload to the site &amp; that''ll be good for him.  Did not send temp yet, because he wants to have his comp up &amp; do everything together.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-30 17:56:03', '2022-11-30 17:56:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108300018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000101104002', 'Tennison Barry II', NULL, '11-30-2022:  Tennison sub an RX Quote for:  Vyvanse BRAND (no gen avail yet) 70mg, #30
     - Best price I could find was thru RXSaver at Publix for $353.66
     - tt Tennison, he gets a memb disc at Costco that bring it down to $270 = considerably less than anything I can find.
     - Did send him the mfg disc site.  But we disc that even the ''cash-pay'' patient option req a "other coverage code" & how if you are a ''cash-pay'' patient, I have no idea how you have that code.  He appreciated my at least sending him the info.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-30 17:42:01', '2022-11-30 17:42:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108300013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102743002', 'Sandra Anderson', NULL, '11-30-2022:  Sandra called.  Nahla wanted some guidance, so she brought me in.  I helped Sandra see if/how lab orders from her annual appt might be covered.  We disc diff components to her healthcare & how each takes care of diff things.  Disc Planstin = Prev Only & to be clear w/doc off.  Doc gave her sep orders for quite a few things including a DexaScan.  We disc bone density is part of the MEC plan, but the DexaScan includes more & therefore I have not seen them cov it under the ''prev care''.  Sugg she ck DexaScan''s site, because they sometimes advertise places in your area that are having $99 sale for the scan, that could be one way to have that done at a discounted price.  She went to one of the clinics that come around and had a bunch of tests done.  Some items she listed will be duplicates to her doctor''s orders.  Sugg, since she already paid for those, to have the doc review & let her know if anything duplicates the curr order.  Talked about how to handle cov labs, & ''cash-pay'' labs.  Then let her know Planstin makes final decisions on what is & is not part of the MEC plan.  Made sure she has their number & Nahla trans her directly to Planstin.  I let Sandra know, they have some new people, so if something they tell her seems contradictory to my info, please let us know and I''ll verify for her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-30 15:54:15', '2022-11-30 15:54:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108305008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066564305', 'Robert Mitchell', NULL, '11-30-22 Best guess at income was $100K and still gets a big APTC. Anthem Bronze Mountain Enhanced X HMO 7450 for HSA Bronze/HMO - Premium$1,520.92,  APTC $1,243.95. All set for 2023.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-30 15:53:30', '2022-11-30 15:53:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108302017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102743002', 'Sandra Anderson', NULL, '11.30.2022 Sandra called.  Nahla wanted some guidance, so she brought me in.  I helped Sandra see if/how lab orders from her annual appt might be covered.  We disc diff components to her healthcare & how each takes care of diff things.  Disc Planstin = Prev Only & to be clear w/doc off.  Doc gave her sep orders for quite a few things including a DexaScan.  We disc bone density is part of the MEC plan, but the DexaScan includes more & therefore I have not seen them cov it under the ''prev care''.  Sugg she ck DexaScan''s site, because they sometimes advertise places in your area that are having $99 sale for the scan, that could be one way to have that done at a discounted price.  She went to one of the clinics that come around and had a bunch of tests done.  Some items she listed will be duplicates to her doctor''s orders.  Sugg, since she already paid for those, to have the doc review & let her know if anything duplicates the curr order.  Talked about how to handle cov labs, & ''cash-pay'' labs.  Then let her know Planstin makes final decisions on what is & is not part of the MEC plan.  Made sure she has their number & Nahla trans her directly to Planstin.  I let Sandra know, they have some new people, so if something they tell her seems contradictory to my info, please let us know and I''ll verify for her. NT for CA', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2022-11-30 15:37:13', '2022-11-30 15:37:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108305003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108303013', 'Megan Lewis', NULL, '11-30-22 Meg is 39 and just got laid off. Referred by her employer Margaret Randolph. Cobra will cost $570.68 and she was paying only $220+. She will likely get approved for unemployment at $742 a week which means $38,584 annually until she gets another job. She was earning about $101K she said. She takes some migraine meds which are expensive but can be split into two generic drugs for Treximet. She rarely goes to the dr. otherwise. She sees Amy Rule Caldwell for mental health and she shows in network for Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $0 Ded for 2023. I sent her instructions to create account, choose me as agent and then Apply for 2022 and again for 2023.  In 2023 her cost will be $193.18 and APTC $153. She will work on it now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-30 15:36:23', '2022-11-30 15:36:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108231093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097899002', 'Amy Jones', NULL, 'Amy called in for lists of in-network labs and radiology centers. I sent via email. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-30 14:15:54', '2022-11-30 14:15:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000108289059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108245009', 'Catherine Surdoval', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-11-30 13:58:08', '2022-11-30 13:58:08'),
