  ('zcrm_1579374000107482003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064061001', 'Aryeh Dori', NULL, '11.18.22 - This member called in about his plan. I explained what his Care+ plan consisted of and he insisted that he can now get a membership through Zion. He stated they offered him a better plan with a lower rate. He said that when we raised our prices it is because MPB just wanted money but I told him that since Zion''s rates went up, ours had to as well. He insinuated I was lying to him as he said Zion told him that we raised our rates "just because". Aryeh started asking me pricing questions so I sent him to his agent. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-18 11:59:57', '2022-11-18 11:59:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107477034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107471065', 'Rebecca Bradford', NULL, '11-18-22 Rebecca came to me via Erin Brennan. But, Rebecca''s income will be dropping from $60K to $20K in the new year once she loses spousal support. So, she qualifies for a huge subsidy of $745. She''s with Kaiser and wants to keep them since all of her drs. are there.  She''s not currently a C4 client, so I sent her the instructions to create her account and choose me as her agent. I sent to her 2 Kaiser plans to review for $1.52 - $14.89. No health issues but no money here soon. She''s paying $570 now with a $8500 ded. She''ll let me know when she''s ready for the next steps with the account.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-18 11:57:13', '2022-11-18 11:58:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107441073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000070067085', 'Kayla Boettcher', NULL, '11-18-2022:  Kayla & Matthew are still perm AK residents, but are traveling a lot right now.  She knows they will be 2 weeks in the 49428 zip area & was thinking they would try to find a PHCS ntwk Fam Prac doc for their annual appts.  We went over the search tool, HCBB to look at quality of care, etc.  She was talking about how diff this has been, esp in AK.  I let her know we may not have to worry about ''ntwk'' next yr, but it''s not for sure yet.  She''s going to try to decide and will call us late Dec if they decide to go that route, to conf if the no ntwk is taking eff 1/1/23.  I let her know it''s not guaranteed.  We did find quite a few options in the zip we ck''d.
     - We went over doc must bill, all srvcs must be in ntwk, prev ONLY & how to sep., etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-18 11:34:37', '2022-11-18 12:55:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107441068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081677010', 'James Benjamin', NULL, 'Left another message for James to call me back if he wants to cancel. I mentioned in the voicemail, today is the cutoff, otherwise he will be billed for December.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-11-18 11:34:18', '2022-11-18 11:34:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107464023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081151002', 'April Kocsis', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-11-18 11:13:52', '2022-11-18 11:13:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107441063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058356861', 'Peter Byram', NULL, '11-18-2022:  Katie & Peter are thinking of cancelling their memb.  Their advisor is no longer active & I am working with her sister-in-law, so we talked a bit about why.  They have some up and coming exp & their $2500 IUA seems too high.  None of what they think they need to have done is on the books yet, so I trans her to Patti to see if going to a 1k IUA would be an option.  However, they want counseling which ours might not be enough (not sure they''ll get much more w/any other ''ins''), have derm issues she thinks will need to be taken care of, & a third item she couldn''t remember.  Let her know we are here to ans questions if they need.  She mentioned coming back after they have these things done & I reminded her that they would then have pre-x items to work around.  She''ll leave Patti mess if she doesn''t catch her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-18 11:02:11', '2022-11-18 12:56:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107477029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033866102', 'Susan Muenchen', NULL, '11-18-22 Susan was prescribed something similar to ColoGuard for preventative. I''m not certain if that is included in wellness since it''s not a colonoscopy. I told her to call the Concierge Team for that and for her thyroid meds. I also told her to complete the colon test in Nov. if it''s included. If not, then wait to do it until Jan. 2023 when the network restrictions have been removed. She will do that. All set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-18 10:57:54', '2022-11-18 10:57:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107477021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033866102', 'Susan Muenchen', NULL, '11-18-22 Susan is cancelling Sedera $1500 and to be $389.22 and moving to SECURE $1000/$325 to keep her costs down. I told her to hold off on her wellness visit until Jan. 1st and removal of network. She said no problem. She''s enrolling now and then we''ll cancel her PSDHC next. She will not bother with the conversion process. This will begin Dec. 1st 2022.  I waived the $100 for her since already a member.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-18 10:44:45', '2022-11-18 10:48:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107477016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002887157', 'Trevor Mickelson', NULL, '11-18-22 I talked with Trevor and the new company he''s working with might have some options for him and he still has his health ins license. So, he''s going to choose something new on his own moving forward.  I just showed him how to complete the cancellation form.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-18 10:34:05', '2022-11-18 10:34:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107477011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004455005', 'Carleen Andersen', NULL, '11-18-22 Carleen called C4 and reached a knowledgable person finally who was able to remove the Friday plan and select the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 Bronze/EPO for premium $329.20,  APTC $184.10 and her cost $145.10. She''s all set now for 2023.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-18 10:27:16', '2022-11-18 10:27:16'),
