  ('zcrm_1579374000107392026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001107434', 'Lauren Peterson', NULL, '11-17-22 Lauren is choosing Cigna Connect Flex Silver 4100 Silver/EPO for $47.85. Income will remain the same unless the economy gets better. She is super nice and super appreciative of my help.  Premium $759.23, APTC $711.38. All set for 2023!  She will send her partner Jeff to me to discuss MCS since he''s paying about $400 per month for a crappy plan. He may or may not reach out, she said.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-17 16:52:14', '2022-11-17 17:01:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107392021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107380008', 'Brady Litts', NULL, '11-17-22 Brady Litts is 26 and earning about $65-$70K. He doesn''t have insurance since it ended with employer back in June 2022. He just start working for his previous employer again PT and no benefits. He bounces back and forth between them and another company. He has high blood pressure and they are sorting out his medications now. He tests his blood pressure on his own and is hoping he can use the virtual healthcare app to get their advice on his medication. He used lisinopril but not sure he''ll keep using it. It only costs about $4 mo. Lives in Evergreen in Clear Creek County. He did break his leg last year but it''s all good now. I explained the pre-x clause to him. He''s choosing CARE+ since W2 employee and I told him to pay for wellness on his own. He only goes every other year. He chose $2500/$165 banking on not having any issues moving forward and saving $600 year if no health event. Enrolled with ACH bank draft and he knows he needs to do Welcome Call after Dec. 1st. He also needs a deep cleaning for dental ASAP. So, I will send him some dental options. He''s not tied to any dentist at this point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-17 16:06:49', '2022-11-17 16:06:49'),
