  ('zcrm_1579374000107392008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779146', 'Shana Larsen', NULL, '11-17-22 Shana is 45 and husband is 51. She got Sedera through her employer/association. They had Sala Summit Plan for the wellness and couldn''t get Sedera without Sala (sp?).  Her cost is $804 with the $500 IUA. Her husband broke his tibia and fibula on 2021 in a snowmobiling accident. He was recently cleared  by his dr. a few months ago. He had emergency surgery when it all happened and the entire thing cost around $200K! He now has some discomfort in his ankle from the rods they put in and that might have to be addressed at some point in the future. She understands the pre-x clause if they switch to SECURE. They are both W2 employees but Shana does have a remote 1099 job on the side to show proof of self-employment. Other than the broken leg, they don''t have health issues, no tobacco. Husband takes 2 meds, 1  gabapentin and 1 escatalapram. 1 for restless legs and the other for depression. Her new employer will pay 50% of her cost. I''m asking Dania if we can keep her on Sedera but through MPB now instead. Rod gave me permission to do so and told me to inform John Kach. Now awaiting to her back from Dania.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-17 13:29:49', '2022-11-17 13:32:47'),
