  ('zcrm_1579374000107032088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094737002', 'Faviola Meschi', NULL, '11-14-2022:  Faviola called.  When she purch this healthcare option, they went in & looked for her doc, but after taking her daughter in for her ''prev care'' appt, it''s all been declined as out-of-ntwk because they see the doc at a facility that is not in-ntwk.
     - IF this off is not a part of the ''prev care'' she wants to cancel because that''s why she has the plan.
     - Was denied coverage by Planstin as our-of-ntwk with no ntwk discounts 
     - She called Planstin & tt Carmen who let her know the doctor is in ntwk but NOT at that location because it''s an out-of-ntwk facility
     - She called the doctor''s office who referred her to the facility
     - She called the facility and they had no information for her
      - She called PHCS who told her the doctor is not in ntwk using the NPI#s
     - She sent  over the communication, EOB, etc., for reference
     - I tt to Ivette at Planstin who says they''ve had a lot of difficulty with this facility and that''s why they have a "caution" sign next to the doctor''s name (which is not something visable on the list that was originally sent to her).
     - I reached out to Michele thinking it''s important for Tony to know what''s happening, & sugg a few things:
          Make sure people know the search tool is a ''GUIDE'' and can change at any time
          Note the address listed for the doctor and make sure the patient is aware of any limitation (the caution sign).
          Mention to members to call the Concierge Line before non-emergency care to make sure they have the current information and can get guidance for whatever they are trying to do, to make the most of their healthcare and not run into issues like this one.
          Our guidance would have included verifying with the facility they are a covered office prior to the appointment & if the office cannot be certain, to please call PHCS with the doctor & facility NPI#s for confirmation.
     - The member has already approached the billing office for ''cash-pay'' discount = 20%.  Currently the least she owes is $838.40.
     - I called Zion to see if their advocacy team can help her bring down the price any further, but had to LM. 
     - I tt Faviola & let her know I''m trying to see if we can get any further assistance.  I also mentioned we may go to a diff type of billing, where there is no ntwk to try to save this member.  It''s not guaranteed, but we hope it will take eff 1/1/23 & it might fix this issue for next time.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-14 11:41:52', '2022-11-14 19:20:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000107032083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079659002', 'George Hasrouni', NULL, '11-14-2022:  George called.  He has an emerg ambulance ride (& ER?) visit in Oct.  He presented his ''Planstin'' card, so we went over that''s ''prev care'' ONLY.  They have not had their ''Welcome Call'', so I sent an invite & went over good to have entire fam on call so everyone understands how to present.  He''ll see if he can arrange that & get a date sched.
