  ('zcrm_1579374000106700003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000689078', 'Kim Gangwish Zahorik', NULL, '11-9-22 I sent Kim 3 plans to review side by side with Cigna. She had endometrial lining cancer this year at stage 2. She had a hysterectomy and will be monitored 4x per year now and still monitored for 5 years.  She thinks her income will remain the same for 2023, at least for now. She also was told by Cigna that the ded is separate from mop and you have to pay both, ie. twice. After reaching ded, they are telling her the amount starts from $0 to then reach the mop. She''s calling them again to see if she gets the same answer. I''ve never heard this to be the case. That would be insane!
UPDATE - 2nd Cigna Customer Service Rep told Kim the same thing that her mop starts at $0 once she''s reached ded. This is totally bogus. She''s calling them back one more time with the chart and information I sent her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-09 11:31:41', '2022-11-09 12:29:08'),
