INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000106505008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034039274', 'Rochelle Booker', NULL, '11.8.22 - Member called to cancel her plan. I advised her that I would transfer her to Jeffrey who could assist with this process. Rochelle got frustrated when I mentioned that she may have to leave a vm but that Jeffrey would get back to her when he was free. I transferred her over to Jeffrey. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-08 08:33:44', '2022-11-08 08:33:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106505003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103922002', 'Gary Zoz II', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-11-08 08:31:03', '2022-11-08 08:31:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106502003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034039274', 'Rochelle Booker', NULL, '11-8-22 Called to update her account from the Sedera email. I quoted her the new price that I think will take effect Jan. 1st, $565.97 at $1000 IUA. She also has an expensive pre-diabetic medication that is super expensive that she needs pharmacy coverage to get a good deal. I told her to contact MPB Concierge team to price it out or to try the Apex/RCI card since that is an insurance card. I''m not sure if it has a pharmacy benefit attached or not. She feels good again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-08 08:29:43', '2022-11-08 08:29:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106460003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075870001', 'Paula Peck', NULL, 'After getting in touch w/spouse Anthony, I will rerun 11/22 pmt w/new CC info.  I will put Anthony''s email as primary &amp; add his contact number per his request.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-11-08 07:51:58', '2022-11-08 07:51:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106440008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105428002', 'Steven Vertz', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-11-08 07:47:14', '2022-11-08 07:47:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106440003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105486012', 'Jorge Trejo', NULL, '11.8.22 - See ticket from Bern Phillips. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-08 07:08:27', '2022-11-08 07:08:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324115', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098327002', 'Cindy Gordon', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Cindy sub a tkt asking about how to sub a ''med need'' for going to the ER &amp; having follow-up care/tests.  ILM on the # she supplied &amp; asked her to call the concierge line so we can walk her thru the process.     - CA

Cindy called back.  I sent her temp for sub a ''med need'' to Zion &amp; walked her thru the process.  She knows there''s a 6mos deadline &amp; will start the ''need'' as she gets going.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 17:11:10', '2022-11-07 17:39:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106404026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107490001', 'William Stohlton', NULL, '11-7-22 Will is 37 and daughter Cadence is 6. They were referred to me by Springs Insurance Brokers!  I will have to find out who they are. His insurance offered by work is crazy expensive at $300 per week, $1200 per month for him and his daughter at this new job that he started today. He''s working as a contractor for the company, so he believes it 1099. He has VA benefits which he uses for anxiety and depression medications. His ex-wife also has a plan for their dauther but he''s required to have one per the court orders. I let him know SECURE would be considered secondary to her other ins. I sent him the video to further educate himself on how and why it works. He originally said no to MCS and then once I showed his the traditional insurance plans with C4, Friday Health was the cheapest at $418.38 with $8700 ded and mop, he went back to MCS. He''s ready to enroll in SECURE $525/$1000 for Dec. 1st start date. Also simplifies process since the price will remain the same at $525 in 2023. He will not have to reapply. This was right in his budgeted range. We will reconnect on Nov. 18th at 4:00 pm.  He also wants dental and vision, VSP and not sure for dental which to offer yet.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-07 16:42:42', '2022-11-07 17:02:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324105', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102402002', 'Rabih Sabra', NULL, '11-7-2022: Tkt asking about functional nutritionist - sent e-mail in reply.  See below.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 16:23:30', '2022-11-07 16:23:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080584001', 'Zubair Niazi', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Zubair called.  He does not understand the plan.  He''s stuck on ded.  I tried to explain IUAs and I don''t think he ever understood.  He kept saying $7500 before anything paid...  I tried.
     - His wife''s endoscopy is tomorrow & will be <1k.  He knows he has a $2500 IUA.  He''s unsure when this started, maybe it was pre-x, maybe not.  He''s decided they are going to get this done now & not after their anniv date of 12/1/22 & not worry about poss pre-x implications even though the first tier of 25k/sharing on a pre-x IF needed begins in then. 
     - He called a second time asking about the OptumRX, Vision, Dental, ded, etc., on the back of his Planstin card.  Went over ''prev only'' & sent him a copy of his post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail for ref re: what is cov & pointed out the healthcare.gov site link verbally.  He''s in the car & I didn''t want to completely confuse him any further than he already is.  
     - He mentioned his maint RXS & I asked if he''s ever called us for pricing.  He argued "we" told him how expensive ours pricing was & we couldn''t help him.  But, once we discussed the OptumRX on the back of his Planstin card, he could hear "we" are not who he''d talked with.  He may call us about a week before he''s ready to get his RXs, to see if we can help him find the form to sub for an RX Quote from MPB.  It was a very difficult concept for him to understand.
       I''m not sure he caught any of what we discussed.  Maybe it''s the language barrier, his being sure he understands so he cannot hear adj to those thoughts?  He is definitely confusing w/ins, as well.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 16:22:46', '2022-11-07 17:59:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106404021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107986163', 'Sylvie Bloch', NULL, '11-7-22 Eli is helping his wife get coverage. He''s 68 on Medicare, son is on school insurance and Sylvie needs insurance. He earns about $250K, so way too much for APTC. He likes Cigna as a nationwide option. His wife is super healthy. The prices for the worst plans were starting at $681.28 with $8500 ded and $9100 mop. After he looked at those and saw how terrible they were, I mentioned MCS. He wants to learn. He had to go to vet appt. I''ll send video and we will talk tomorrow at 3:15. She was on Bright Health but that''s no longer an option.  The C4 system was trying to suggest a Kaiser plan for $700. MCS will be half of that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-07 15:28:12', '2022-11-07 15:28:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000023155119', 'Timothy Cook', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Timothy called about Sedera''s e-mail presenting Sedera+ &amp; has questions.  It''s after hours for the FL office, so I trans him to Patti''s line &amp; he will LM.  He''d like to understand what they are saying &amp; what he needs to do.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 15:13:11', '2022-11-07 15:13:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106369044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104757002', 'Mary Johnson', NULL, '11.7.22 - Welcome call complete! ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-07 14:48:27', '2022-11-07 14:48:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105311002', 'Sandra Ganas', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Sandra called about 16min after her sched Welcome Call time.  She apologized.  She''s going to resched for a Fri when she''s not at wk.  Sent her new invite.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 14:38:39', '2022-11-07 14:38:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106369039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093632002', 'Adrian Piazza', NULL, '11.7.22 - Member''s wife had a question regarding the paperwork that Zion Healthshare is having them fill out for a need. I warm transferred her to Zion to get the answer. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-07 14:17:50', '2022-11-07 14:17:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106369034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103360002', 'Richard Bender', NULL, '11.7.22 - The office staff from Celebration Pediatrics called to find out what type of insurance this is so we went through the cost sharing info and Planstin info. Come to find out, the pediatrician that they are looking to see is not in the network. It doesn''t appear that the Bender''s asked us for a list of providers at all. Hopefully we will hear back from the Benders so we can give them some guidance. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-07 14:12:35', '2022-11-07 14:12:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106369029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000070370117', 'James Batch', NULL, '11.7.22 -James called about how to present himself as self pay when speaking to the hospital. We went through that and if James needs any assistance he will give us a call. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-07 14:08:49', '2022-11-07 14:08:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106404016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054986001', 'Ken Trombley', NULL, '11-7-22 Enrolled in 2023 KP Select CO Bronze 6500/35%/HSA,  $734.25 Full Cost, APTC $604.04,  Anthem Dental Family Enhanced $23.38, Plan ID 21032CO0410035-01, Acct # 3515102660. He''s all set for 2023. I reminded him to make sure to check on his payments moving forward in 7-10 days. He has accounts set up with each to check on them. He believes he''s all set.  We checked to make sure Dr. Uusinarkaus and Dr. Rosenbaum are showing the network. Kaiser and Anthem looked to be the only options to keep both doctors. So, he kept his same plan as last year. Also updated his income which turned out to be nearly identical but coming in differently than before. 2023 he will take about $10K from Bella Panini and $42K from rental property. He was thinking it would be $46-$48K but not when he includes everything inclusing wife''s small income. Total was just over $54K.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-07 13:38:27', '2022-11-07 17:31:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106401016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102507011', 'Ron Akins', 'No longer wants to be an affiliated', 'Ron sent Kelly F and email stating that he no longer wants to be an affiliate with us. Patti B responded to him with an link to Agent Termination Request.  I followed up by sending a text with the same link.  If we do not hear from him in 2 days, we will terminate his affiliation.', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2022-11-07 13:37:12', '2022-11-07 13:37:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059281121', 'Dechen Hawk', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Laura called.  Ketamine therapy has been suggested for her chronic pain.  Zion told her to call us.  The pain may be linked to her PTSD, so Zion wasn''t sure it would be considered ''medical'' & thought we might be able to sugg ''mental health'' options.
     - Got her to the MAP program pg & explained the counseling progarm, how it works, etc.  She doesn''t think they''re willing to chg counselors, so prog may not fit.  Plus, I wasn''t sure it would be the right type of program for Ketamine therapy.  Did let her know Mizz & Sull is usually willing to reach out to counselors to see if they''d be willing to join the ntwk, so she may try that.
     - Also went over doc letter sugg the treatment is a ''medical'' issue (not mental health) & could sub a ''treatment plan'' for the ketamine therapy to see if Zion would help share.  Reminder her they have a 1k IUA that dir though.
    - She wanted to know if they could get the "same type of annual expense" she had years ago.  From her description, w/Liberty? & a combined $500 annual ded?  I let her know their curr 1k IUA is our lowest.  Went over how IUAs work.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-07 13:31:14', '2022-11-07 14:33:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106369024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099851002', 'Ronald Guerra', NULL, '11.7.22 - Ronald called to check on the status of his open need with Zion Healthshare. I transferred him directly. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-11-07 13:27:01', '2022-11-07 13:27:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106324069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065477440', 'Richelle Entenmann', NULL, '11-7-2022:  Richelle has bad foot pain &amp; called to see how to handle.  She''s seeing her PCP today, so: ''cash-pay'' to her 1k IUA, get det inv w/med coding &amp; receipts.  Then she''ll call us on the backside if it looks like she''s going to want to start a ''med need''. 
