  ('zcrm_1579374000106167031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000052617079', 'Merryl Rothaus', NULL, '11-3-22 Merryl has her surgery coming up on Dec. 19th for her knee/foot issue. So, we''re looking at a Cigna $0 ded plan for at least the first few months of 2023. Then if all goes well she could possibly switch to DIRECT for $295/$1000.  Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 for $554.90 is likely the path she will go for at least the first, so she can assess the success of her surgery.  Her DOB is 11/11/70 and will be celebrating next week. She knows we want to complete this before the end of Nov. and she wants to do so as well. She''ll text me about times when she''s free. Super thankful for my insights. Tired of dealing with Anthem''s terrible customer service with non-native English speakers and waiting on hold forever.  Also, she wants to keep Dr. Robert Leland who looks to be showing up all non-Kaiser plan options. She takes NP Thyroid and shows up in GoodRX for about $17-$20 for highest mg amount and Desvenflavaxine ER with Pharmacy Checker shows up for $62-$85 for 28-100 tablets. She''ll be better off paying cash for meds than running it through Cigna with the high co-pays or full cost via ins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-03 14:22:32', '2022-11-03 14:37:55'),
