  ('zcrm_1579374000106035087', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028522022', 'Matthew DePofi', NULL, '11-2-2022:  LM for Matt - wanted to make sure I document we did get back to him.  He claims we never call him back.  I do think he gets confused on who he''s working with:  RCI, vs MPB, etc.  He''s very confused & has a difficult time helping, this may not be the best fit for him.
     - Mail we had was sent to us due to RCI fwd''ing items when they kept getting his mail back per Kelly F.  I searched & cannot find a Cognito Form w/his new address or any notes on it.  Maybe I''m missing it?  Sent him the link w/chg form so we can make sure all entities (incl RCI) have his new address.  Let him know we updated his files here, but having the form on file would be helpful.  [There are no notes, so although we updated our CRM & Admin123 files, I don''t know if we notified RCI & thought the form could help us make sure that happens too.]
     - Tried to work w/RCI, but get stuck in a loop since I''m not the client.  IF Matt calls, have him tt ''claims'' dept at RCI.  They should be able to tell him why he''s getting bills & why things were not covered & he''s receiving bills.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-02 16:38:29', '2022-11-02 16:55:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106035082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079912009', 'Stephen Wetterling', NULL, '11.02.22:  Called, l/m to c/b and let me know if Liz received the email I sent them w/the HMA information.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2022-11-02 16:31:09', '2022-11-02 16:31:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106018107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083756038', 'Lisa Birkhofer', NULL, '11-2-22 Lisa and I completed her new enrollment for 2023 with Cigna Connect Colorado Option Silver with APTC of $893.09 and her cost $11.13 and full cost $904.22.  Dr.  Jessica Brynn Bare shows in the network. She''s pulling out of her retirement income about $1200 a month but may pull more on occasion depending on her needs. We rounded up to $19.008  which brings her above Medicaid threshold. She prefers to be able to choose her plan and get the APTC. If pulls less for income she will just get money back in taxes instead of owing more money at tax time. She''s very pleased and knows to contact Cigna directly to make her payment in 7-10 business days. They won''t accept pmt on C4. She''s all set for 2023 and remainder of 2022.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-02 15:53:19', '2023-01-04 11:16:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106035071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086715002', 'Nancy Krampetz', NULL, '11-1-2022:  Nancy & David called in together to understand how the ''Prev Care'' works on their plan.  Their daughter Brianna has the same plan, so they will pass along what I taught them, because even though Jennifer went over everything w/Brianna, she''s still super confused.  
     - They were super confused & we had to distinguish between the different components because they were thinking they always present as ''cash-pay''.  Hopefully, they understand better now.
     - ''P''lanstin = ''P''reventative Care ONLY:  All entities/prev srvcs must be in ntwk - we went in to the PHCS search tool together so they could learn to use it.  Doc must bill, ''prev'' care only, etc.
     - Tried to help them see how HCBB wks.  Even though I was signed into the account, using the same browser, on laptops, we could not get the same info to come up = super frustrating on both sides.  It almost sounded like their pages weren''t loading properly?  Gave them an idea of how it works & what to look for while deciding on a new ntwk doc from the PHCS list.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-02 15:46:44', '2022-11-02 15:46:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106035066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105234001', 'Brianna Krampetz', NULL, '11-1-2022:  Brianna''s parents are also members: Nancy called to get info for them re: ''Prev Care'' &amp; since Brianna''s so confused they will pass along what I told them to help her.  (They are all on the Secure Plan, so the info will work for both membership.  See the parents'' CRM file for more notes.)     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-02 15:35:12', '2022-11-02 15:35:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106035061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011716785', 'Megan Friday', NULL, '11-2-2022:  Megan called & her derm let her know she has basil cell (although, a better kind?  So it sounds treatable).  They want her to have a MOHS procedure.  I sent her the temp on how to sub a need to Zion & went over all the details.  It looks like she will meet her $2500 IUA & than at least a little, so we went over how/when ''med needs'' get closed in case they want to monitor her.  She has a $400 receipt from the diagnosis & labs testing the sample she''ll submit right now.
     - Also went over HCBB from my end & e-mailed her the Fair Price of the MOHs Surgery & Derm w/in 20-miles of 80303.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-02 15:33:12', '2022-11-02 15:33:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106004091', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043491714', 'Douglas Bush', NULL, 'Leslie  Jablonski reached out to me about this member, Doug had questions, that she couldn''t answer. Leslie forwarded me the email from the member, and I sat down with John K. we went over everything and forwarded the email to Leslie. I will touch base with her again tomorrow.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-11-02 15:21:26', '2022-11-02 15:21:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106035053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165388', 'Kimberly Baldwin', NULL, '11-2-2022:  Christopher called to see if hearing aid expenses are shareable.  I let him know the Memb Guidelines say those items are not shareable.  He did open his HSA, so I sugg that might be an option, but to double ck they qualify (I think they do, but don''t want to guarantee it).  Also sugg he tt his advisor Wendy Scipione re a very diff product the HMA.  My experience is hearing aids get used pretty heavily & need to be repl.  The HMA could be a resource for the replacement.  Gave him a super short idea of how it works, what it''s for, it''s completely diff, but might be an option.  He will call to discuss w/her.  He''s a super nice guy & easy to work with.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-11-02 15:20:55', '2022-11-02 15:21:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106018102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779231', 'Eric McConnell', NULL, '11-2-22 This is Robin Kemp''s client for all things except dental! She passed him to me for dental since she''s not licensed in CO. He has a bunch of dental work needed for immediate issues such as gum work and possible root canal. He''s been going to Castle Peak Dental in Eagle but they no longer accept Guardian or Ameritas. He thinks Delta Dental might be OK. He also may want to see Dr. Albers (female) who he''s seen at Castle Rock or Tony C. Kardelis at Denver Dental Specialties. I suggested he calls them all and finds out which individual health ins carriers they accept and then I''ll help him find the best plan within those parameters.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-02 14:51:39', '2022-11-02 14:51:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106018097', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025756108', 'William Cranney', NULL, '11-2-22 Dale called to cancel bc he''s getting coverage through work. I left him a vm just now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-02 14:35:55', '2022-11-02 14:35:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106004086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088568002', 'Thomas Parsons', NULL, 'I spoke to Tom per Jeff Kanter''s request. Nice guy, he wants to cancel, because he has too much out of pocket expense on this plan. He''s looking into other options. he was driving and couldn''t go into much detail. I''m emailing him my contact info for him to call me back so we can do a side by side comparison.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-11-02 14:28:50', '2022-11-02 14:28:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106018092', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000035605393', 'Ian McLendon', NULL, '11-2-22 Etta was ready to bail on Redirect bc of so many ongoing challenges to get a few items paid and to communicate with them. She had to resubmit some bills in every possible way, multiple times and still not paid. Only resolved when she was able to connect with Mike Bechtol and now all is well. He told her they no longer use the Spruce app but they have their own app. But, he told her it''s best to send a text to some # for pre-approval now instead of any app. I will reach out to Mike to better understand what''s the best protocol moving forward. Etta was super nice and said she had to lose her cool to finally get to Mike for help. But, she''s willing to give it one more try. She said Sedera has been great, so they aren''t the problem. Moving to SECURE will then bring the pre-x clause which might be a problem since they seem to have some medical expenses now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-02 14:22:40', '2022-11-02 14:22:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106018084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068476142', 'Michael Dee', NULL, '11-2-22 Mike is 56 and Christie is 55 with 4 older kids I mentioned before and 1 new granddaughter! Mike has been self-employed his entire career except first year out of college. He''s a General Contractor. They have about $40K in simple IRA and $280K in variable life. But, they sold one property in Denver in Dec. of 2021 with 8 units. Now they still have 40 units in Denver that value around $3M-$4M, plus his homes mentioned above. They don''t have a trust set up yet and just have an old will. He asked about knowledge regarding Delaware Statutory Trust (DST) which neither Mara or I have heard of. It''s a way to protect against some tax implication when selling properties. Mara them mentioned Irrevocable Life Ins Trust ILIT that she''s familiar with. Mike''s also part of a non-profit (I think with brother who lost 4th child) called Global Orphan Relief.  They are looking for long-term solution for retirement plan, to protect assets and create long-term income stream with little management. Now managing the properties is a full time job still.  They are looking for next steps and Mara will send them an email and we will reconnect when they have some ideas of the direction they want to go.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-02 14:01:31', '2022-11-02 14:02:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106004081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571018', 'Randy Sherer', NULL, 'Patti, handed this member to me to speak to about cancellation. I reached out to Mike Montes (agent). I could not reach him, I will try him back to discuss how he wants to proceed with this member.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2022-11-02 14:00:56', '2022-11-02 14:00:56'),
