  ('zcrm_1579374000105863013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068476142', 'Michael Dee', NULL, '10-26-22 Talked with Mara and she had some great suggestions for his long term financial goals and to better protect them in case of a major health incident down the road and for long term income that they won''t outlive. Setting appt with all 3 of us.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-26 16:03:15', '2022-10-26 16:03:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105863008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068476142', 'Michael Dee', NULL, '10-26-22 Mike Dee called about ERC but he doesn''t have any employees. He asked about the debt program but was asking with a friend in mind, not for him. He''s most interested in financial strategies. His kids are all older and out of college. 2 of the 4 are married already. They have life insurance policy on him for $500K in case something happens to him. His work was built around the trades type of work. They own their home outright, plus a house in Breckenridge outright. They also bought 3 apartments or apt buildings in Denver which they both still manage all of the properties. Those aren''t paid off but they are bringing in cash flow. He''s not sure the balance of debt bc they refinanced them 3-4 years ago. They''d love to get out of managing the properties someday sooner than later. They have a $20K debt of car and another $60K-$70K on another vehicle. They could pay it off, but they are choosing to use their money in other ways. He also has 2 HELOCS, one with $130K balance and the other with $30K. His 2 homes are worth $2.5M and $1.5M. All of the properties will be for his retirement money. Sounds like he''d like something that''s simpler to rely on long-term, if possible.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-26 15:39:38', '2022-10-26 15:39:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105863003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105821012', 'Greg Wayman', NULL, '10-26-22 Greg is an ASHI member. He''s 47 and just got divorced. They have a son with Crohn''s diease that will not be included. Greg''s wife just ended his insurance without him knowing. So, now he''s left without anything. He lives in Omaha, NE. He''s healthy, no tobacco and "no clot shot." He doesn''t do his annual wellness visit. He realized he will need to do a colonoscopy or Cologuard in the future but it''s really not until age 50. He doesn''t have any family history from the sounds of it. He''d prefer CARE+. He was fine with $300 when I quoted him wrong. It''s $240/$1000 which is even better. So, he''s happy! I gave him the ASHI discount of $100 and did it on their site. He understands the 6 month time limit bc his now ex-wife sat of some bills for their son that totaled $125K! The were balance billed and about 1 year past. So, they had to fight them and got the bills down to $3,900! He says waiting made it way more difficult to deal with and fight.  John was able to give him a Nov. 1st start date as well!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-26 15:18:28', '2022-10-26 15:18:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105828020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032206031', 'Bryan Tew', NULL, 'Members 11/22 payment declined 1st notice sent via email &amp; vm - 10/26 10/26-spoke to member he will be updating 10/27-member submitted pmt update I will rerun  10/31 finally got corrected Exp Date from member I will rerun', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-10-26 14:30:45', '2022-10-31 13:19:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105856013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086318002', 'Zachary Weaver', 'Response to email from Traci', 'Hello Traci,

Here is the Member Timeline that I believe will help:
Feb 10, 2022 - An email was sent to confirm March 1 start date with a link to schedule the Welcome Call after her start date
March 1, 2022 - Start Date
March 17, 2022 - One of Concierge Team Members spoke to member to schedule her Welcome Call
March 17, 2022 - Email was sent out with the Welcome Call link to schedule Welcome Call - Email was opened
No Welcome Call was ever completed
During the Welcome Call we go over all the items that you discuss when enrolling the Member, just in more detail including checking the PHCS Network for any MEC members.

On to the bills:

On the bill for $150.00 has printed at the top of the Invoice   " Important Message: Out of Network".
When reviewing her profile, I do not see any notes suggesting that she called the Concierge Team to see if Drs Hill and Chapnick were in the PHCS network prior to her scheduling her appointment nor do I see where she completed her Welcome Call.
After further investigation I checked to see if they were listed in the PCHS network, and they are not.

Planstin is the only portion of any of our plans that is Preventative Insurance (just like the ACA) and to be compliant the member/patient must verify their provider is in network prior to their appointment.  

With any Preventative Insurance, the member/patient must stay in their perspective network and tell the physician that the visits and the lab work must be preventative only.  This way everything is taken care of.  

At this point, it is up to Planstin to determine if they are going to pay an Out-of-Network Provider.  

We have done everything on our end to help engage the member to take the necessary steps to ensure the member is successful with us.

Let me know if there is anything further I can do.



Michele Rebal


Infrastructure  Manager
Agent Development Director
1761 W Hillsboro Blvd #104
Deerfield Beach, FL 33442

Click here to contact me!
