  ('zcrm_1579374000105384013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094176105', 'Stephen Klein', NULL, '10-19-22 Just spoke to Laurie with RMHP to get my commissions which started June-current. 4 months have been paid out at $20 per month, $80 owed. Laurie sees me as Agent but it''s getting paid to MPB and to 506 SW 1st St. Boca Raton, FL and phone # on file is 561-288-4398. She referred me to call UHC at 866-235-4095 and I reached Terry who is trying to help, but not very helpful. She can''t find me under my NPN or Rod''s NPN. I was contracted back in 2013 with UHC and 2015 with RMHP.  She will supposedly call me back tomorrow.  I''m owed $20 x 2 for Celeste Styles as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-19 16:28:57', '2022-10-19 16:28:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105389008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084833002', 'Heath Honbarrier', NULL, '10-19-2022:  Heath called and wanted to know if there was a fee for a cc pymt of his mo cont (he chg''d it online).  I let him know it''s 3% &amp; now he wants to chg it back.  He is LM for Patti so maybe his VM will catch her early tomorrow.  I''ll also put a note in his Admin123 file.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-10-19 16:02:41', '2022-10-19 16:02:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105389003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105322002', 'Christopher Ambrosio', NULL, '10-19-2022:  Christopher will upload his proof of self-emp tonight, but is very nervous about what he''s supplying.   For his comfort, he would like to conf it qualifies, so I sugg he call tomorrow and Patti can confirm for him?     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-10-19 15:36:20', '2022-10-19 17:30:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105384008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763104', 'Bryan Lonergan', NULL, '10-19-22 Bryan''s membership just went from $175 to $240! So, after us talking through the good and bad of increasing his IUA to $5000, he''s confident he won''t need to tap into it. If so, he will be able to pay the $5K if something bad happens. He''s not worried about multiple health issues in one year. He''s willing to take the risk before he ages into Medicare. He''s already paying cash for most everything he needs such as his wellness visit, medications, PT, etc. So, it''s really for something really bad. He asked about options for when he''s Medicare age. I explained the HMA and he really likes that idea. He won''t do it today, but understands it takes about 1 year to grow to a point where it beneficial to take advantage of.  He has plenty of legit ongoing costs that will be relevant, including a medication. He''s going to tally his costs from this year to help determine the best level to choose from.  note from Wendy', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-19 15:10:54', '2022-10-20 08:06:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105384003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059964144', 'Christopher Loven', NULL, '10-19-22 I talked with Chris about adding his dauther whose 20 at CSU now. New cost would be $625/$1000. Sounds like CSU''s plan is $290, so nearly identical for monthly cost. He was asking for a little coaching for his upcoming wellness visit. His doctor wasn''t on the list that the Concierge Team sent him, so I told him to call the provider or show them the card to confirm. The dr. is at Boulder Medical Center, so likely in-network. I let him all the ins and outs of wellness with coding, network, billing, etc. He also knows if he has a visit with the same dr. later for non-wellness to pull the card and pay the cash price at time of service. He gets it!  All set for now and will decide about daughter later.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-19 14:52:59', '2022-10-19 14:52:59'),
