  ('zcrm_1579374000105315013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083353002', 'Maribeth Liska', NULL, '10-19-2022:  Charles called concerned  because he hadn''t rec''d an e-mail conf of his cancellation.  He doesn''t have enough funds, so needed to make sure the pymt on the 20th will not be pulled.  It looks like Patti''s taken care of everything, but I don''t see a conf e-mail in Admin123, so I just sent her a quick conf Teams chat.  I assured Charles Patti will make sure he''s all set & there will be no pymt on 10/20/22 because those funds would be his Nov cont & she''s cancelled him for that date.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-10-19 11:07:17', '2022-10-19 11:07:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105315008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099710012', 'Shane Lebsack', NULL, '10-19-2022: Linda called.  Shane is headed in for an MRI on his knee.  It just started hurting recently (so doesn''t sound like a pre-x).  It''s $800.  She''ll call after they have the pymt receipt &amp; we can begin a ''med need''.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-10-19 10:58:58', '2022-10-24 08:41:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105317003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105316001', 'Susan Brady', NULL, '10-14-22 Susan asked many great questions after reviewing her medical records. She is recommended to go a colonoscopy every 5 years bc they found benign polyps. I explained if they code it as diagnostic bc it''s sooner than the recommended 10 years that she will have to pay the $1000 IUA. If coded as well check then no cost via ACA compliant items. She sees an endocrinologist every year to check  her thyroid and all clear. She gets mammo every year and has cystic breasts, all clear. She does skin checks every year and all clear. She does have anxiety which was severe before her new life changes. She''s working towards getting off those meds now. She has slightly high cholesterol and may not be relevant soon as well. She had slightly high blood sugar levels after a long reunion/party weekend. She gor re-tested by dr and A1C came out well. So, all set on that front. She does take atenolol for anxiety and Zymbalta but moving off of both of those now as well!  Had a cardiologist visit for anxiety Oct. 29th, 2020 and all clear! Also falls before the 24 months, so off the record for pre-x. No further visits and clean bill of health. Joined SECURE $1000/$325 for Nov. 1st. Super careful to make sure she reviewed and revealed anything that''s of possible concern. All set and feeling good now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-19 10:46:45', '2022-10-19 10:46:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105282036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100759002', 'Lucie Lalonde', NULL, '10.19.22 - Lucie called in with 3 scripts for pricing. I sent that info to her via email. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-10-19 10:43:50', '2022-10-19 10:43:50'),
