  ('zcrm_1579374000105070038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779307', 'Dillon DeJesus', NULL, '10-13-22 Came through Big Wave Lead system. He put in his 2 week notice to leave his job on Sept. 21st. He doesn''t have a job now so will qualify for Medicaid. I instructed him how to select me as his agent and how to proceed through the app to get accepted into Medicaid. He''s keeping my information in case he has any problems. Sounds young and just wants most catastrophic coverage. He''s fine with Medicaid.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-13 13:06:34', '2022-10-13 13:06:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105076043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086225001', 'John Donovan', NULL, '10.13.22 - John called in because he is going to need surgery soon and wanted to know what Zion''s opinion was on going to have his surgery in Tijuana since it is half the US price for the surgery. I advised John that I was unsure of what Zion''s stance would be on this and directed him to ask Zion. I answered a few more questions regarding the member portal for MPB and sent him his log-in info via email. I then warm transferred him to Zion so he could speak with them about having surgery outside of the US. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-10-13 12:35:29', '2022-10-13 12:35:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105076038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000090935002', 'Tracy McKinney', NULL, '10.13.22 - Tracey called just to verify that she is presenting as self-pay for her breast ultrasound and presenting her Planstin card for her mammogram. I verified that with her and she had a couple other little questions that I answered. She is knowledgeable about how to use her plan, which is  a win for us! ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-10-13 12:32:40', '2022-10-13 12:32:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105070033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042857185', 'Molly Palmer', NULL, '10-13-22 Molly called and is super frustrated bc she tried to go to her annual wellness visit yesterday and they rejected her card and she has to reschedule. She tried calling the Concierge and was not able to reach anyone. She called me at the end of the day. I just called her back and left her a vm. I called Jennifer who will help make sure she has the right card and explain how wellness works. Molly mentioned really needing the visit bc it sounds like she has some health issues. I just suggested that Jennifer reminds her of virtual healthcare for immediate help at no cost.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-13 12:29:14', '2022-10-13 12:29:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105076033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095912017', 'Alicia Hutchens', NULL, '10.13.22 - Alicia called in with questions regarding finding a therapist through the MAP program. She attempted to find one through MAP''s website but had no luck. I advised Alicia to speak with the MAP program directly via phone and they should be able to assist her in finding a therapist. I gave her the MAP phone number and direct transferred her. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-10-13 12:24:49', '2022-10-13 12:24:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105039044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097338001', 'David Bamberry', NULL, 'Received a response email stating that he would look into comparing the prices for E&amp;O outside of what we offer.', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2022-10-13 11:38:19', '2022-10-13 11:38:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105096003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000101897001', 'Daniel Kane', NULL, '10-13-2022:  Daniel called to make sure I could see his proof of self-emp.  I can see 2 items in Admin123.  Also conf his eff date = 11/1/2022.  Told him next step is a ''Welcome Call'' after his eff date &amp; sent him an invite.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-10-13 11:27:11', '2022-10-13 11:27:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105070028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105093002', 'Elizabeth Koster', NULL, '10-13-22 Elizabeth is joining now CARE+ EC $1000/$420. Husband will remain on employer insurance. Employer coverage was going to cost them $2K! Then different option the employer would be taking $195 out of paycheck per person, semi monthly so, about$1600 for the family. So, this is WAY better for them and they don''t have to worry about a doctor network. They understand wellness is self-pay not reimbursed, but still better off.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-13 10:19:29', '2022-10-13 10:19:29'),
